my body and size that really get to me.\n\nNow, whenever I bring it up, he says I “can’t take a joke” or that I’m insecure. And maybe I am. But I also think there’s a line — and being constantly made the punchline in your own relationship doesn’t feel like love to me.\n\nSo… AITA for being upset and not being able to laugh at his jokes anymore?", "prompt_sha256": "79525ac46c3c445bc0b8d0bc5cf133089d0f426cca563b18461b774bdea3751f", "body_sha256": "fcb74fbe08dd6e9e534e794448ac7c84537637d941e3e6951f3d5593b2bef53f", "previous_prompt_sha256": "65be16f5a98d7eef6b8c2b9223f1c2afdc0abd5bd1f6562c5d9d4a44bcd5dabe", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P049", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (22f) have been with my bf Neil (23m) for two months now,we used to be casual friends before dating,our relationship is amazing,he is caring, loving and I love him so much. \n\nThe problem is his ex,she was two months pregnant when he left her but niether knew at the time, and then fast-forward to now, she is almost 8 months pregnant (and no he didn't leave her for me or anything,they had their personal issue, when she was 5 months we started dating) \n\nHe was over their relationship emotionally way before breaking up with her so he had no issues moving on quickly with me, but he told her he is gonna support her with the child and he will provide her with money if needed.\n\nNow I don't mind this, I am actually proud of him for not ditching her but my problem is, how often she needs him,I get that she is pregnant and probably very emotional, but why does she need emotional support from my bf specifically when she has her own family and friends and support network?I kept these thoughts to myself but yesterday she called him crying and saying she needs someone to be with her at the moment because she was on the verge of a breakdown and no one was available to help her so she reached out to him. \n\nHe went to her house panicked because he thought something might happen to the baby,she was fine but just emotional form the hormones I guess,he came back two hours later and I sat him down and talked to him, I explained that although I do not mind him being involved in the kids life, I don't like him being involved in her life,she could've called anyone but ultimately called him, why?, I told him I didn't feel comfortable that he went alone to her house to comfort her and that this incident might make her pull this thing more. \n\nHe told me I was an AH for not understanding, he told me he went there for his baby not for her and that my feelings didn't matter in this situation because no matter what, she was the mother of his kid and he would take care of her, I told him I just wanted him to put boundaries with her and he told me to fuck off and went to the bedroom, and is now giving me the silent treatment. \n\nI understand she is going through it rn but I don't like how she keeps asking my bf for emotional favours, it makes me feel like there is still something lingering between them but also that could just be her pregnancy hormones and this behavior is normal, Idk, AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "0199c41fa419510f3543e75fc8172c5957def76bb0b5c28bb394d623f3852082", "body_sha256": "66f97aa6e73541a32f178204d1aa4e9812578c753005373e3f88f24e3f563db0", "previous_prompt_sha256": "a360f9595a6a586d608397be51e361730f4886aa8bcef08ab7a5be60973b4257", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P050", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nBackground: I (27F) have a daughter Eleanor (5F) her father (Nolan 30M) and I broke up 2 years ago after cheating on his end. We keep it civil, and I try to push my feelings aside for Eleanor's sake. \n\n\r  \nMy brother Josh got married this past month, and his at the time fiance had asked for Eleanor to be the flower girl. She was super excited about it, especially since she got to wear a beautiful dress for the occasion. At the ceremony, Eleanor was supposed to lay the flower petals, walk around the groomsmen in the first pew and sit with me in the second pew (The aisle was on the right side and I was sitting on the left side; the right side was saved for parents). \n\n\r  \nAt the ceremony, my daughter was doing so amazingly until she ran out of petals about midway thru the aisle. She stopped and looked around really confused. I honestly didn't know what do to since, if I were to get up I would either have to walk in front of the ceremony or walk from behind in front of my soon-to-be SIL. I was just about to get up, when one of Josh's groomsmen, Blake (28M) walked up to her, held out his hand, and led Eleanor in the direction she was supposed to go. Blake brought her to me, I thanked him, and the wedding continued on. \n\n\r  \nPresent: My SIL got her wedding pictures back and she's been posting them all over Instagram and Facebook. A couple of these pictures are of Blake holding Eleanor's hand walking down the aisle and walking up to me. My mother (Nolan has her on social media), took all the pictures of Eleanor to make one huge post of her. They of course included some of the pictures of her and Blake. Nolan screenshotted these pictures and sent me a text saying that I intentionally humiliated him. I told him I wouldn't do that to him on purpose and that Blake went on his own accord because I couldn't get to her without walking in front of everything and messing up my SIL's moment. Nolan won't listen to me, in his words, \"You made me look stupid in front of your family,\"\n\n\r  \nI feel guilty about this. I could've led Eleanor myself but I didn't and now Nolan is embarrassed because of me. My mother and Blake say I'm not an asshole but they have biases. I think I am the asshole, so I decided to post here to get unbiased and different opinions. I just want to know if I need to go out of my way to make a huge apology to Nolan since I want to remain civil for Eleanor's sake. AITA? \r  \n\r  \nI'm adding this for context since I feel that it should go toward my judgment. I've known Blake for a few years now, he and my brother are really close, and he shows up to family parties on occasion. Nolan knows him from these parties and others. At Josh's reception (I had Eleanor a babysitter pick her up after the ceremony) Blake and I did dance and spent most of the night together. My SIL posted a lot of pictures and there were pictures of us dancing and smiling together. I can be 100% sure but there is a chance Nolan saw these, and it could've affected his actions. ", "prompt_sha256": "ab79fa8a0ead8ce984e30e81960e0f003513dd3c1f142f5528134a20c5a1e759", "body_sha256": "f4836c07e5b2106511b654f4b525b3a41b916bf9d73d75afe903f90bd223c98f", "previous_prompt_sha256": "d0a295a676ebe6659382bbaa5dd4c7a0ca55a3d1e10d9006e3e2e97692a238d4", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P051", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI'm not gonna lie, I'm a slacker with work. After getting wayyy too bought into the \"girlboss feminism\" kinda shit and overworking myself for jobs that underpaid me to prove something to who knows who, I decided that my career goals were gonna be... Getting paid as much as possible for as little work as possible.\n\nIronically, this attitude has brought me way further in my career than the grinding and hustle culture ever did. I've strategically picked work that made me an expert in a very niche and very well paying engineering field, and put me in really high demand. I go to interviews regularly with the internal energy of \"You need to convince me to come work for you\" Which helps me in negotiations way more than the \"Please please hire me!\"  energy ever brought me. \n\nSo as much as I call myself lazy, it took a lot of strategizing to get there. Plenty of privelege too, I'm not trying to discount that either.\n\nSo that background out of the way; I work from the office 1 or 2 days a week, and \"work\" from home for the remaining days. I share an apartment with my boyfriend who works from home full time. \n\nBut honestly, I front-load all my work on Monday and sometimes Tuesday. Then throughout the rest of the week, I'll send out the rest of my work piece by piece and respond to emails and Slacks. But honestly my usual week looks like:\n\n8 hours Monday\n\n1-8 hours Tuesday\n\n1-2 hours Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday \n\nMeanwhile, my boyfriend, who works in the same industry, has this schedule -\n\nEvery weekday: 9-10 hours plus evening calls \n\nWeekends: Called about \"emergencies\" more weekends than not. If he's offline they'll call his own cell. \n\nHe gets frustrated with it sometimes, but whenever I've encouraged him to look elsewhere he says stuff like how he hates interviewing, and \"better the devil you know\" \n\nI've mostly stayed out of it even though I feel like he's doing himself a disservice.\n\nBut we've been having this ongoing conflict, he'll act super judgemental when I'm doing stuff other than work when he's working. \n\nJust comments like how I'm being paid to get an ass, when I was weightlifting one afternoon, or asking if my boss knew I was doing \"arts and crafts\" on the clock when I was making some custom stained glass pieces to sell on Etsy one morning. \n\nAfter a few more times like that I got so annoyed I snapped at him that I didn't know why he was acting like such a bootlicker, like did he really want me slaving away for no damn reason or was he just jealous? Because if it was the latter, that's a him problem... And if it's the former, I was kinda judging him for sucking company dick. \n\nI know it was a harsh thing to say but I was honestly fed up with him talking shit whenever he saw me not working. Stuff has been so tense since.\n\nAITA for slacking at work when we're both working from the same apartment, and for my fight with him?", "prompt_sha256": "4653f161dbcf953490981cf52ac15cd99133c5072c85a02598883f893624583d", "body_sha256": "b2dd5531eeac214f5c7a1e7c84b9921a9506616242440d9e4add36d1b14021a9", "previous_prompt_sha256": "8953e9c9f749506c4f6bb9984a97e9158f0ad7725902cd525d4d930aa8438cb3", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P052", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI am getting married in 2 weeks. It is important that I have the people closest to me there, my sisters and their children being some of the most important. \nMy father and one of my sisters got into an altercation 3 years ago and have been estranged from each other ever since. While my sister has made it clear she intends to avoid him and wants no trouble, my father who harbors an immense amount of vitriol and disdain for my sister implicated that if she was going to be there, he would bring security detail with him to hold him back from “going at her.” In response, I told him that if he did not trust himself to behave in her vicinity then perhaps it would be best if he came to just the ceremony while she stayed for the reception.\nIn response, he said he’ll come to neither and someone else can give me away, namely my “matchmaker” aka the common friend (F) that my fiancé and I happen to share who had no direct hand in us getting together.\n\nNote: he has not contributed a penny to the wedding, moving, any of my post-secondary schooling, and in the two years of knowing about my betrothed, has barely found the time to meet with us twice despite having ample free time. Aita?", "prompt_sha256": "9e2fb8cad71e06028b678043e54bae4f4e18ae5eea1cb0e138342874189c576a", "body_sha256": "9800df39daa241be21a0dd0ca46c7b1c2a33fa1d868aaf3337d9fb7d9631759d", "previous_prompt_sha256": "4c9b2a975bcffee6214636291564573c91ef173ebcc77d3aedba39da99052f39", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P053", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHello everyone.  Bare with me as this is the first time I have ever posted. My younger daughter suggested and showed me how to get onto this site.\n\nSo here is the problem.  My oldest daughter has been a flight attendant for 22 years and have been with the same airline that whole time.  This marks the 22 year in a row that we have not been able to spend any holidays with her either.  This was her dream job and she was so excited when she got the interview and hired and made it through training.  We knew at the beginning that she was going to miss some holidays as she got settled in but now she is pretty high up in seniority.\n\nI called her the other day to tell her about our Thanksgiving times and she said that she signed up to take that time since it would be holiday pay and over time.  I was not happy with this and told her that she needs to stop putting her career and job over family.  I told her that it would be nice if for once she would actually spend some with us during the holidays. In turn she told me she was doing this for her future.  She was trying to desperately get her condo paid off so that she didn't have that big payment hanging over her head.  I got mad and told her to do what she thought was right.\n\nSo the question is. Am I the asshole for wanting to spend time with my daughter and enjoy the holidays with my entire family?\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nAdditional info:\n\nShe is so much different from us.  She always has been.  We live out in the country in the middle of nowhere.  We are blue collar.  My husband works in a factory and I in an office.  Both of my other kids are happy with this kind of life but she has always wanted more. She went to college and got a degree while she waited to hit the age she needed to apply for her job. She lives two hours away from us and comes home if we are lucky every other month for a day or two and then hurries and just goes right back. We go see her for a couple of days on the off month.\n\nI have hated her job since 9/11. Maybe now it's irrational but I have always had a fear of losing her since that time.  That time was the worst.  We didn't hear from her for three days.  We kept waiting to have someone show at our house to give us news we feared. I have told her this a million times over but she constantly tells me I'm safe. I get that she is happy and loves what she does.  But I feel that she just refuses to find any kind of balance in her life.\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nEdit.\n\nA lot of you are asking why we can't just reschedule.  We have.  On many occasions we have tried to reschedule many times and all we get is Sorry I gotta work.  Sorry I gotta work.  Sorry I gotta work. So it's not like we don't try.  I did show my husband this post and he is laughing and so am I at this point.  We both decided that at this point we just need to be done.  She is going to do what she wants. You all are right.  Twenty-Two years of this.  I should be used to it at this point. We decided to try  something to prove my point.  We are just not going to contact her .  Lets see how long it takes to see if she realizes that we aren't talking  or visiting. And if we don't hear from her for a while then I guess she is just happier without us. I'll give her her space.", "prompt_sha256": "ad1f664bafa8b5bcb74b2fa0f0f4d5f5a1f18bd4df4cadca1b723787febb01e1", "body_sha256": "255ad4b8abeeffabd021edee01bceb0083da3925c9ddb09acad799cd081d4cb6", "previous_prompt_sha256": "684c61d77bc55f03299eaf7dfde5b2198ee9796499803fb0bdf7123e2a1c93da", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P054", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThrowaway because my main has a lot of personal info and even though I don't care if my friend sees this, I don't want some person who thinks i'm the AH (which I may be) to dox me or something. English is not my first language so I apologise if I make any grammatical or spelling errors.\n\nMy friend, Lucy (18F) and I (17F) have known each other since middle school. From a young age Lucy has developed a habit of asking me for answers to test papers or assignments and I always gave them to her but also made her understand the questions and answers.\n\nJunior year I told Lucy that I would no longer help her cheat since now our grades had an actual impact and consequence but she always managed to convince me to help her, especially since we have been friends for so long. This is one of the reason why I may be an asshole btw, since I helped her kind of develop this habit of depending on me.\n\nShe would always leave a few questions and this basically ensured that the teacher wouldn't find out she was cheating because at the end of the examination, our marks would be different so the teacher wouldn't have any reason to doubt us. (I get As and she writes enough to get Bs)\n\nThis is our last year in school and at the start of this semester I told her that this time i would definitely not help her. I told her that enough was enough and that if she got into a good college with the marks she got by cheating, that would not be fair to someone who worked hard. She said she understood and that was that. In the first two major examinations she got Cs and I guess her parents were not happy.\n\nLucy then begged me to help her again and would constantly badger me every day by spamming my socials or when we meet up with friends. I told her I no longer wanted to talk to her but she would just not let things go and even threatened to reveal some secrets that I had trusted her with when we were younger. \n\nSo 2 weeks ago, when we had an examination and she asked me for answers I gave her the wrong ones. She left some and somehow got marks for that but her overall grade was F.\n\nWe got the results yesterday and till that moment I thought I was justfified in doing what I did to get her to stop harassing me but when she got the result she started sobbing. Like full on crying and i felt so guilty. She later called me a lot of names and told me I crushed her dreams and I feet so bad but I know I did what I did so that she would stop with the cheating. So i'm confused. Am I the asshole?", "prompt_sha256": "5176e4f40a171f970c874e3b4ba40415a13d292d7c70fc39fe0e9816257306d2", "body_sha256": "916aef0ed4233d65a96de50b6bf90495e02be28e3c60d1ffad65bd91f7443a14", "previous_prompt_sha256": "36e127929f37b584209dff1d85115893b8a1645cb2a504a793d52f45962b8f47", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P055", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI’m currently 33 weeks pregnant and my due date is in early February. I planned on having my mother &amp; my baby daddy in the room for labour and delivery. I asked my mother if she could not tell anyone that I’m in labour when the time comes. I would like to have the time in the hospital with just my baby daddy &amp; my baby. I’m a first time mom and I know birth can be an exhausting/ traumatic thing so I’d like that time to unwind and be in my bubble without people coming in and out overwhelming me. I’d make an \nException for the baby’s grandparents but that’s it. My other reason for this is I’m supposed to deliver during cold &amp; flu season. Newborns immune systems are very weak and RSV in babies has been very bad this year and I’m not comfortable risking it. So I asked my mother if she could not tell anyone when i fall into labour. She told me no, she’s at least going to tell my grandmother. I told her no, if she does that then my grandma will come to the hospital, and I do not want any visitors other than the baby’s grandparents. My mother said “you’re such a tool. You can be the one to tell her you don’t want her there than” I said I’d gladly tell her. My sister, who’s been listening the whole time, then said she’s coming home around my due date to be there at the hospital whether I like it or not. I told her I’d have her escorted out. My mother started to get angry and yelled “why can’t you just be normal?” \nI said it’s cold &amp; flu season then my sister said “that’s just an excuse. She’s just being like this for the sake of being like this” I told my sister to shut the fuck up and that im sick of her attitude towards me all the time. (My sister has always been very hateful towards me and loves to shoot passive aggressive &amp; direct insults at me for no reason) my father then cut in saying im the only one with an attitude and that it’s not normal to not want any visitors at the hospital. I said it’s very normal and they’re all being very rude. My mother said I just don’t want my baby to be celebrated. I said that’s not true I just don’t want any visitors of extended family for the first two weeks of the baby’s life. My sister then said “I guess if she doesn’t want her baby celebrated then we don’t need to throw her a baby shower to celebrate it.” \nMy mum then agreed and said they’re not throwing the baby shower for me anymore. (My baby shower is supposed to be in three weeks) I honestly had nothing else to say at that point so I just sat there for a few minutes then walked down to my basement apartment &amp; started to cry. I now plan to tell my baby daddy and baby daddy only when im in labour, and it will be only him in the delivery room. I am not going to tell my mother this to avoid another argument like this. I just don’t understand. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "3a2398c3d91a2ec1b3210b0cb0eb550a11abe3a1457ddc84bd26b52878f7d91a", "body_sha256": "812b74ba8383675fd2719e95daca35c1111f01c0a49771caf24f0a5897bd8062", "previous_prompt_sha256": "3434bcbfd73bd99fe8775304f0475769757c89990829b977bb5360ff56f1ad4c", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P056", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis one's a bit silly but bear with me. 2 days ago my mother (56,f) went to a restaurant and took home take out. Rice, vegetables, and some kind of meat I think. She proceeded to leave it all in the car over night and all day the next day. It got to close to 20 degrees Celsius all day and the car was in direct sunlight. She took it in yesterday and got mad at me when I asked was she seriously going to eat that. Well today when I was out she ate most of it. Both me (29f) and my sister (25f) are quite emetophobic (a disproportionate fear of vomiting roughly) and I had asked her not to eat food that was more than likely going to give her food poisoning as being stuck in the house with that is my worst nightmare basically (I'm here to watch the family dog for the day as he is young and can't be left alone and I can't go back to my apartment with him because I have 3 cats). She lashed out at me asking did I think she was stupid, she's not a 2 year old, she knows what she's doing ect. I told her that in some cases food poisoning could literally kill a person (she's just getting over covid like 2 weeks ago and still not back to full strength) and she threw back in my face that I wouldn't care if she died, I just don't want her to throw up. She yelled at me more, belittled me, made me feel like an idiot for seriously worrying about her getting bad food poisoning because that food was in hot temperatures for a long time, and she made me question myself. So AITA for asking her not to?", "prompt_sha256": "1f37c54a05f44eeb6d8610e1786fb73fe73742536ca961aa566fe997b777cec1", "body_sha256": "933d2ca2c4c8fe5d183f937abf542eaf981cf0be1bb1e1878b05b5398455286d", "previous_prompt_sha256": "202f59e5db4a0307597f12b1e00e781982761daf955c656b733179152865c535", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P057", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI 26f and my husband 31m live in a 2 bedroom apartment. For the past thanksgiving my in laws usually rent an airbnb where we all pitch in but due to bad financial decisions we cant this year. Since its the week of thanksgiving husband and i just planned to get our favorite take out and spend it together but in law called and said they wanted to do it in our home, not taking no for an answer. My husband and i are gamers and all our crap that is worth thousands; consoles, pc, games, figures all displayed. we have to fit 5 people and 2 children into our home. The first and last time they visited some stuff broke because of the kids and everything we owned was being touched. Also I have a pet bird now, which you cant cook the turkey a certain way or it could harm my bird, my mil also sages/cleanses the place without being asked and lights a candle which is deadly for my pet. \n\nWhy can't you just rent a cheap airbnb? Last thanksgiving we got banned, mil didnt clean up after herself and left the room a complete disgusting mess. We vow to never rent anything with them again\n\nWhy cant they do it at their place? Its a disgusting mess. Let your imagination run wild and yes its exactly like that. I had to teach my husband that some of the things he was taught isn't normal and unhygienic.\n\nI think im the AH because its just for 1 day, theyre family and they're the ones bringing food but part of me says no because its my home that i dont want to be uncomfortable all day. AITA?\n\nEdit: i just wanna update and thank you all for the advice. I've put boarded my bird to a local bird place, thank you for this great advice! MIL is currently throwing a tantrum and ignoring everyone. Even her husband thinks cooking the food at their home then bringing it here is unnecessary but is too scared to say anything so its on me and my husband. She's has NEVER been said no to, so this is the calm before the storm.", "prompt_sha256": "ee216489f20b087bf48a4984c6bd521d6084cfea9115b1fe3a4d4712713cf78f", "body_sha256": "652e2b18e1aee5d9ca6aa1712eef637ce7365ce9329251b2c8a65e1374aa54c0", "previous_prompt_sha256": "10f6f9d980b677fdfae352a6eeb996d987fc6209ac17b750a2410bf7ad9bfdb4", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P058", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (M24) live with my disabled sister \"Elena\" (F24) and my girlfriend \"Mia\" (F22). Elena was born blind, so everyday I help her pick and dress her clothes. I don't feel troubled by it because I have been responsible for helping Elena since we're 12. Our parents always worked full time to put food in the table and they also needed to take care of our younger siblings. I have a great relationship with Mia and love her very much, the only real fights we had up till today were caused by her jealousy towards Elena.\n\nElena writes romantic stories, I don't have enough time to read her books, but I'm proud of her efforts and that she's earning some money with her stories. Before Elena started writing, she thought she would never be able to have a profession.\n\nYesterday Mia told me she was feeling jealous, and asked me to start to help Elena dress instead of me. I denied it, because it would make Elena uncomfortable, and I questioned Mia why she started to feel this way now. She said to me that the last story Elena published contained a scene where the female lead (who's a blind girl) gets turned on by having her \"boyfriend\" help her dress and after this they sleep together. I think Mia is being unfair by indirectly accusing my sister of nurturing sexual fantasies about me.\n\nBesides, Elena is wearing underwear when I help her and it doesn’t take more than 10 minutes, so I don’t think it’s really a big deal. Elena has been consistent in her whole life about only feeling comfortable in being helped by me or our mother.\n\nMia now says I’m emotionally cheating on her with my sister and  that I should stop helping her to dress, or send her to live back with my parents (I would never kick Elena out). Once again, I think Mia is being unreasonable, just because I have a close relationship with my sister it doesn’t mean it is emotional cheating (we just talk about our days, hang out, watch movies together, etc).\n\nIt’s beyond me how Mia managed to convince two friends we have in common and my own father of her position. My mother sides with me and Elena.\n\nSo here I am asking you — fellow redditors — am I the asshole?\n\nPS: English isn't my first language, so please forgive any mistakes and throwaway account to preserve our anonymity.\n\nEDIT:\n\nI talked with Elena about this post and she allowed me to share more regarding her health, but I won’t be naming anything.\n\nElena can’t walk (although she can feel her legs) and her body overall is more weaker and fragile than an average female body would be. Therefore, everything she does, she does it using her arms and it is very tiring, so keep in mind that she’s limited by her stamina as well. My job is basically carry her around to the bathroom, to the bathtub and to her wheelchair (she can use the bathroom and bath alone). We arrange things so she can have the as much privacy and independence as possible. But after all this she's too exhausted to finish dressing herself alone.\n\nShe's doing physiotherapy to increase her strength and stamina, so in the future she will be able to do more than she does today.\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nUPDATE:\n\n[update link](https://www.reddit.com/user/throw_away65535/comments/ycg8vw/update_aita_for_helping_my_disabled_sister_dress/)", "prompt_sha256": "1ecf8da5ecf19969f2969cbfd67712b48780afe0cb6f01f235fb96987345fbf0", "body_sha256": "41022318f157b5f040379e5ab1f72f542e6d212e358f7b2d409a653cbc981d32", "previous_prompt_sha256": "3873daad5c489ee2ddbf215c967fad269c113717b1f33812c9e08b80b6d80a43", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P059", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (29F) and my brother (25) went home to our parents house for new year.\n\nGrowing up I always felt that my brother is my parent's child. Although they were \"vocal\" that they love us both and there were no favorites. I beg to disagree but I understand and don't really give an f growing up.\n\nOn holidays, my brother would get a new gaming console while I only get a book, or we would get the same phones but he would get an extra money so he could date his gf. When I graduated college, they gave me a car, and I am so happy until a few days later when they also gave my brother a car because they say \"to be fair\" to both of us. When he graduated college he was given an international trip as a gift. Then, I didn't bat an eye but I am keeping score.\n\nIt does not stop there, when he moved out, they gave him a place as a gift because he \"would have a family and they will live there\", and I had to rent an apartment on my own because they say \"when I marry, my husband will provide me a house.\"\n\nFast forward to this new year, my brother arrived earlier than me with his girlfriend that my parents has just met. I believe they have already bonded while I wasn't there because when I arrived, they seem to be close already.\n\nDuring the dinner, when my parents were giving gifts to both of us, as this is our new year's tradition. My brother was given his gift first, he opened it and it was a brand new latest model phone. When he opened the box, his girlfriend said \"wow that's the color I liked\". I think this was heard by my parents, because instead of giving me my gift, they gave her the gift and said to me \"she'll appreciate it more than you and you are more than capable to buy yourself one\". I thought the gf will not accept it because it was mine and had my name on it but she instead opened it and looked really happy. This made me really upset that I walked out in the middle of dinner and I went home.\n\nMy family was bombarding me with messages saying how rude I am and that I do not respect them and that I should apologize to them all. Aita?", "prompt_sha256": "7629c0f20bb42d5ee5b42f1285fa7edc719458fe0647c332db2d697dfc90d0e5", "body_sha256": "6797dfa09f9856d3fe8d8ff574d4ed9b01d3a99d4707cdde3db2f05f75b47a19", "previous_prompt_sha256": "a9e4198f85dc6c882dc14a763799b1636d63d31251e454dab821acae8ed90335", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P060", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (35F) was raised in a family that honestly is pretty messed up. Reputation and wealth always comes first for everyone and well-perfection is the only answer. I’m not even joking lol.\n\nI have a brother (Oliver-19M). Everyone adored him and he was definitely favoured growing up but he’s been through some shit that caused him to act out A LOT. \n\nMy mom had enough of his behaviour and kicked him out when he was 16. He‘s been staying with me for the past three ish years.\n\nWhile living with me, he managed to get his act together as I put him in therapy to help him and I kind of realized that the whole “perfection” thing my family drilled into our brains is kind of what was causing him to deteriorate so much. He goes to a good university, is in a sports team and even has a part time job. His mental health is still a work in progress and he does have bad days but we’re working on it. I’m proud of him in all honesty.\n\nAnyways, my parents were aware that Oliver was with me but only contacted him a couple times in the past years. I would say I get it because of how stressful it’s been but I don’t. That’s your son for fucks sake.\n\nWell, a few months ago, my parents decided to divorce which hey good for them. Should’ve happened years ago but whatever. Ever since, my mom has been trying to convince me to let her talk to/hang out with Oliver. This extreme switch up isn’t good for him as he relies on stability a lot and I told this to her. \n\nShe started crying when I did and said that she’s his mother. I kind of rolled my eyes? and said something like “what a great mom” sarcastically and she cried even harder. \n\nShe said she was sorry for kicking him out but she just didn’t know how to deal with a “problem child” anymore. It wasn’t her fault etc.\n\nI didn’t think she was really getting my point as I’m more annoyed by the whole perfection bullshit she never shut up about (even I have problems with that) but I let her rant. \n\nThen I told her straight up that I wouldn’t and couldn’t help her with Oliver until he said he was ready (even then idk if I’d encourage him) and that she needs to live with her decisions.\n\nShe practically called me an asshole and said she was his mom-not me but I just ignored her. It’s been a while now and I haven’t heard from her and I feel a little guilty.\n\nWhat right do I have to keep a mom away from her precious son is kind of what’s been going on in my head (it’s what she said as well). AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "cd619d2fed3c10c10c93d7fd54cdc84ec48326c8ab431f3f928d3d82aaa34aa2", "body_sha256": "57de5a1a85bf2759311dcbe61c135f7af7e742ba0a352348a1d9efcf320b8504", "previous_prompt_sha256": "392187eed4575a817b97ef88a24b99c56a001678abb7b65992b9119a42c22cc9", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P061", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nTo set the stage I’d like to point out that today I bought myself the AirPods Pro 2 for my birthday as a gift to myself because my previous ones were malfunctioning to the point that I could no longer use them anymore. I’ll note that these have twice the noice cancelling capacity of the previous model, and as I’m sitting here typing I have a big box fan in the window on full speed and music in my AirPods. It works really well.\n\nToday I came home from work and my husband asked if I had to stay late, I told him that I didn’t but that I finally broke down and got new AirPods because the old ones kicked it a while back. I said it was my birthday soon so I just wanted a little something and that if he wants to he can skip getting something else for me (we share finances, so while I could have labeled this a personal purchase I was offering to say we each paid half and he didn’t have to worry about it if he didn’t want to), because I know $189 isn’t super cheap (down from $249 so I got it on sale). This part he was fine with, and even said that he still wanted to get something for me.\n\nI told him I was going to go and try out the noise cancellation and other features. Cut to an hour and a half later, and I’m listening to music and reading my book. Totally forgot I left noise cancellation on when it didn’t need to be. My husband comes in and looks angry, so I turned off noise cancellation and asked what was wrong. Apparently he’d yelled from the kitchen several times to ask if I had any opinions about dinner, and then eventually got mad and decided to make whatever he felt like (I’m fine with that, I’ll eat it) - he did make enough for two. \n\nHe’s mad at me now, and he said that if I knew the noise cancellation was so good that I wouldn’t hear him yelling for me then I shouldn’t use it. I argued that the noise cancellation was half the point of getting the nicer model, and that he knew I was going to be testing them and that noise cancelation was a feature I’d be testing out. I said that I was sorry he shouted a bunch and felt ignored, but that I also hate when he does that and he knew that I’d be hearing impaired while I played with my new toys. He got annoyed with that and said that I should be available audibly when I’m at home, because otherwise he can’t get my attention unless he waved his hand in my face - I said he could have texted me at any point and I would have come down/texted. \n\nHe said it was a dick move to intentionally not be able to hear other people in your house, and then went to eat his portion of dinner outside and left me inside. I really feel like this is blown completely out of proportion, but I reached out to my best friend and she said she’d be pissed if her husband was gaming with headphones and ignored her because he couldn’t hear her. I tried to say that it’s not ignoring if they can’t hear you, but she said it sure would feel like it. So now I don’t know, because I specifically said what I was going to be doing. \n\nAITA?\n\nEdit: I did not say that half the reason I bought them was to block him out, just that a huge part of why I bought them was for the noise cancellation that I was playing with and testing out on day one when this all happened. ", "prompt_sha256": "7dd6d1e2ab035e123ee931d4efec6a875187687623640f7f5c1185042b72df9f", "body_sha256": "e7f099c8cd74461a8c2efdd4c73a6690c509850f988447e538949e4ed6030ebf", "previous_prompt_sha256": "335a6b18247355048fc01b3e3adea781f21be673b2936d886a7ab9e6007b4274", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P062", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSome context: 15 years ago my wife and I weren't doing good as a couple, we almost lost the house because i couldn't care less about it and i was depressed (I'm doing much better now thanks to therapy and meds).\n\nWe fought hard to stay together, and have been happy for easily 10 years, my wife took hold of the finances, at her request, and i transfer her my pay every two weeks, i keep about 20$ a month for myself. Even bonuses i send to her.\n\nRecently, she was snooping in my phone, i asked her why and she said she wants to see what I'm spending money on, so i took my phone out of her hands.\n\nIf she would've said she was looking for something specific or she was just bored i wouldn't have cared, but she was basically investigating me. She hasn't spoken to me since. It's been two says.", "prompt_sha256": "483900861e3941d5d5f773e27a7870e55f11059324e55a7e65b4da8c9a00bba0", "body_sha256": "3bba5b21550a2007cc689bb1cc7fa3cc6256d4e1128ec225cc08546d034e5f8f", "previous_prompt_sha256": "f25332c3711ac4b1792c2cbeab0f5f05f420255fa90579c0589bddd43cab792e", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P063", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI purchased a house 5 years ago and always rented out my two bedrooms to two quiet roommates. My girlfriend moved in and after a year in november, we decided to stop renting to roommates so we can have our own space\n\nMy girlfriends mother and profoundly autistic brother were evicted from their home after it sold, so the plan was for them to purchase a travel trailer and find a spot for it to go.  They purchased it, but didn't find a spot in time and are on waiting lists for a few spots so they had to park it in my driveway april 1st.  This was just supposed to be them renting a pad in the driveway.\n\nApril 1st they had to stay in the spare rooms, so they could get the trailer ready for them, sure no problem.  This turned into three weeks, until I told them they need to move in so I can have my home back.\n\nEvery day, her brother has been in the house all day, I come home to both of them in the house every day making dinner and I honestly just don't want to speak to anyone but my partner after work.  \n\nThe problem is that I can't have any alone time in my home, there's always noise, or someone sitting in my living room.  They're over imposing and I'm unable to confront it without feeling like I'm being rude.  \n\nWill I be the ass hole if I tell them they need to move by July 1st?", "prompt_sha256": "f37f92b0cac760b83b45fab3dc7f11c78f15283bf0bc16acc1bd5ad1b43bbd26", "body_sha256": "99a83a4a14c310581ff0ed5f629d2716b6610d6df1adbda82e622076d050a3af", "previous_prompt_sha256": "3f279830ecd749d21ee2eb931885e6f63e7c4b411b92eb01b3f42801c3356c4d", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P064", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI decided to rent out a room to incoming graduate student at my place since it was tough for me to find an apt out of state when I was starting. \n\n\nI talked with one over zoom, she asked questions and she said she is unsure when she’d be moving so she’ll let me know once she knows. This was July 14th. \n\n\nJuly 29th I haven’t heard anything from her since. I text her asking what day she’d be arriving here. She texts me back and says she’s “planning to arrive late on Tuesday Aug 6th”. \n\n\nFriday August 2nd she asks if it’s okay for her partner to stay for few days because he’s helping with the drive and move. She adds that she’s sorry she forgot to ask this earlier. I text her back: “Yeah that’s fine, when is he flying back? (Edit)”. No response. \n\nSaturday August 3rd still no response. So I text her: “Hi xxx, since I didn't hear back from you... it is fine if he is helping you with the move but just wanted to let you know that he can't stay more than 2 nights.” No response. \n\nSunday. Nothing. \n\nMonday. Nothing. \n\nTuesday August 6th. Until 4pm, nothing.\nAt this point I am annoyed. I decided to text her: “Hi xxx, I think I have waited long enough. Since you did not respond to any of my messages, I am assuming you are not coming to my place but just wanted to let you know that I decided not to rent my place to you anymore.” \n\nOne hour later she says: \n\n“As you know the past few days I've been making a huge life move by packing up all my things, saying goodbye to friends and family, and am currently driving across the country. This is why I forgot to reply to a text message in a few days. \n\nThis is incredibly cruel to use your power in this way. I'm starting a new chapter of my life in this PhD program and now have no home. I hope the rest of the community in this program is not so cold and callous.” \n\n\nI respond: \n“Seriously? xxx, you had days to respond to me and let me know. (Edit) You have not communicated anything with me other than you were planning to arrive late today which I wasn't even sure if that was actually happening because that was before you gave me last minute notice of your boyfriend coming as well. (Edit)\n\nLike you said, I know you are starting a new chapter in life and packing things and moving etc. but guess what, I have done that too and texting to let people know of my whereabouts was not that hard. \nAlso like you said, I am cold and callous but you should know that you need to learn how to communicate with people. \nYou said \"your power\" but I did not claim that power. Please know that that power only became a power because you left me uninformed. \nAlso next time instead of responding back the way you did, maybe simply explain what happened and try to negotiate. I was left with no answer from you for days and it was not only unprofessional, but also disrespectful of me and my time. (Edit)” ", "prompt_sha256": "9e5bb9a302296796869f4708f3e1c08dc1ece067bb411162821d2545f85111f4", "body_sha256": "6fe7e1db0006bdb5251efb856e509e6104242c6f8229507e3511a7608ec99c39", "previous_prompt_sha256": "3dd123cff68cb3d31a4e46348b90b1ef2d6253c5b5f7f78012e76e8389c25743", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P065", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nA little background story to understand the issue: my mother was always very hardworking but after my dad passed away we had a difficult time and also not much money. We (my brother m19, my mom and me w22) made little vacations but it was never really far away. But we dreamed about a travelling to Iceland. We watched documentaries, we planned our trips and we even made posters out of photos from magazines. It was our little hobby as a family. It was clear that we hadn’t enough money (yet) but it was our thing to dream about. \n4 years ago I left home and went studying. My mom got a better job and started saving money for this trip (which I didn’t know - she wanted it to be a surprise for my brother and me). 1 year ago she gifted my brother for his birthday a trip to Iceland with her and me (which I was very surprised about but absolutely happy). She told us that she know has enough money to book the flights (we had to decide the date) and every activity we dreamed of. Sadly and very shockingly she passed away soon after. After a while I talked to my brother and we agreed to do the trip when travelling is possible and we wanted to honor her by bringing something from her to her dream destination. \n\nNow the problem: my cousin (her parents and her are very close family) has struggled a long time due to her partner. Now they have split and she (w26) lost her home (now lives by her parents) and he owned the car she was driving. Her parents only have one car that my uncle needs for his work. She has a really hard time and I’m very sorry for her. Because it takes long to get to her job by public transportation (30 minutes longer for each ride) - she needs a car. She asked me to lend her the money from my mother. The thing is - she asked for money from a lot of people from our family in the past and she did not pay it back fully (sometimes nothing) ever. I’m fearing that if we give her the money and we will not see this money ever again. And it’s something so special from my mother.. I don’t know - I don’t want to give it away. \n\nMy brother also didn’t wanted it but now he (and I) get a lot of insults from our other family members. She told everybody that we don’t want to help her because we want to have a luxury vacation and how unfair this is. Even my grandparents expressed their sadness about our behaviour. I don’t know if it’s really the right or wrong thing not to lend her money because we want to use it for vacation?", "prompt_sha256": "64484f375f460169edfb9680f35aa546afabb6328c543d75d297ede1596b06db", "body_sha256": "98b900a99734493ad7194be9daa976af1027fcda6ba0c77962d9d6e6488427eb", "previous_prompt_sha256": "38190fbc3cb5aecba6e7c801927723448d11d5279a868491f11cca3038268ace", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P066", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy son has had a boyfriend for a year and a half now, it's always been pretty obvious.\nHe'd always be touching our son (not inappropriately or anything), the BF would sometimes greet our son with \"hi handsome\", they would spend significant amounts of money (for 16yos) on presents, my son baked treats for him, they hung out all day and came home with bags full of stuff of Valentine's day, they kept \"accidentally\" falling asleep in the bed together, and just treated him way nicer than his other friends, etc etc. \n\nOur son sat us down saying he had something important to tell us, this kid doesn't take anything serious so we got worried thinking it was something bad. He just came out as gay. I started laughing and said \"duh\" and my husband chuckled and went back to scrolling his phone. We thought he was joking as obviously he was already out \n\nMy son got upset about our reactions. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "c79dd27f9f64f24134b8bc176839ef1106e19f2cb4f033625ff2c77f0dfdc4ac", "body_sha256": "52fd536bb8c343f8b831a4f33996c244ab0adf3517dfbedb7ad2747ae7dff4a1", "previous_prompt_sha256": "c7d71c530209b8b5e4885198b4e898f23aece595bbb99eebcbc2ad7c9f67241a", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P067", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy(27) gf(24) has a group of friends that really love going clubbing and she gets invited to go clubbing almost every week. \n\nI don’t want my gf to go to the club, because I worry she might get drunk and something bad will happen which will be out of her control. Also, I have some trauma because I experienced something like this in my past relationship, so this stresses me out a lot.\n\nI explained my feelings to her many times, and she already went to club on multiple occasions. Last time I tried to explain to her, she got upset with me and said, “what’s wrong with me going to the club, I just wanna enjoy with my friends, I can do what I want”. Yes, it’s true, indeed she can.\n\nSo last weekend she went to the club, so I realized why do I have to care what she’s doing, I called up my friends and we hit up the club too. \n\nShe calls me at 1 am telling me she’s going home, I told her I am at the club now and I am drinking and having a blast. She is furious, she facetimes me multiple times and tells me to go home. I told her no, I want to enjoy with my friends, I can do what I want. \n\nNext day we had a big argument and now we are kind of ignoring each other.\n\nShould I apologize?\n\nAITA?\n\nEDIT (INFO): \nI never called to check up on her.\n\nI didn’t go to the same club to spy on her, I don’t even know which club she went.", "prompt_sha256": "455de1c86a5ff69afb63047102f2c0e5a81b8f0aafd0ec0f2c74ba463534ee9a", "body_sha256": "f7835e930a8ed9b60f68e99297af0095e6869ef153fa26546e88e5a147d589c4", "previous_prompt_sha256": "2bdd25cf4e2818c487fcadae468d1f819e2084c1680d12f560b031a9dd98c9e0", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P068", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo when I go to bed or to my room in general, sometimes Ill grab my furry feline friend and toss him onto the bed from about one step from the bed. My friend saw me do this and she claims its animal abuse. My cat seems fine and doesnt seem to mind honestly. AITA for this?", "prompt_sha256": "93b50f747de5b95dd4944e0dc852af6de9feb48f4b7cac5742c9ba084dc2dad7", "body_sha256": "748e2f7f7c7adf3c61c95f63d3afb8e8bb7fb3be97e998b52677179985a1d9c4", "previous_prompt_sha256": "7977e2d76af963618e03af318cba2e5be631aec63604ee82a311b474395a44be", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P069", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI've (31F) live in a share-house. One of the housemates Jack (M30) has never lived with a woman outside of his mother but likes to say that he is \"aware\" of women's issues and calls himself a feminist. For instance he doesn't agree with the saying \"no uterus no opinion\" because \"It's my job to be informed about any issues that could affect me if I become a father or husband\"...Which is fine until it came to this issue. \n\nSo, like most biological women, I have periods. I however, cannot use tampons or cups due to a condition called vaginismus. It's pads all the time for me - yay. \n\nI also (I know, the shock!) shower during this time! Wow! I prepare a new pad onto a clean pair of undies, shower as normal, dry myself off in the shower, and then step straight into the undies. And obviously check the bathroom for mess. Jack's never complained - nor has anyone else, so I figured my \"system\" was working. \n\nCue today; and I can't shower for 48 hours due to a heart monitor test. I was jokingly complaining about how I was going to \"survive\" without my nightly shower and Jack looked up confused and said \"How is this any different to when you're on your period?\" I asked him what he meant and he said \"well, you can't shower on your period unless you use a tampon\" and I laughed because I thought he was joking - he has shown before that he was at least SEMI educated on women - which he got angry at. \n\nJack said \"wait - well what do you do?\" and I said slowly \"I shower?\" - I wasn't getting it I'm afraid. Jack said \"without protecting **MY** bathroom?\" (he does not own the house) and then went off. Apparently my period is unhygienic, it can cause infection if left on the shower floor, and he was under the impression I hadn't been showering for a week when I had my period or using tampons. I said that due to reasons I can't use tampons and he told me then I'm \"banned\" from showering when I'm on my period which I laughed again at which I did apologise for and say \"I'm sorry for laughing - but the audacity of that statement\". \n\nI told Jack he has no way of enforcing this - nor would I be sticking to this, and he said \"fine. Then every time you shower, you need to bleach the bathroom afterwards\" to which I couldn't help but laugh again - apologising - but saying \"We're in a share-house. That's not reasonable when other people need to shower/use the toilet, and considering I'm sure at least SOMEBODY else pees in the shower, is ridiculous to only enforce on me\". \n\nI brought that up and he said \"nobody does that - I've never heard of that in my life\". So I just had to walk away. Jack's been complaining to other housemates about this and saying that we need to \"watch out for me\" and we all just think he's absurd for 'banning' me, but a couple think that I should just at least try and compromise so I'm confused. AITA? ", "prompt_sha256": "107567f76b04ce2f66e23989892dd4255dda5cf1ab2e2c6984b01820b95b532e", "body_sha256": "4614b1704f73ff708ab7d83552f4a7bd1561c9ba1d31bf76872370c04b4cef96", "previous_prompt_sha256": "026f64a1ecc2921c6454338274267f74e90ad11431628db955295ccb820c80f0", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P070", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nIm currently pregnant and my husband and I own a 3 bedroom home. One is the bedroom, another is his office and game room and the third is my closet. My dream has always been to have a bedroom as a closet/ beauty room. I finally have it and I feel like a princess everyday. However, we have to make room for a baby now. The room furthest away is my husbands office where he can game freely and be as loud as he wants. We both use this room as a home office since we own a business but it is mostly his. We each have a desk in it and the setup just makes sense. However, my closet was custom designed and it brings me so much joy. I always said I would give it up for a baby but now I’m having second thoughts. I think my husband should give up his office since he can game in the living room. We can get rid of one desk and put the other in the living room to work. I would be willing to do my work on my vanity. I know this would throw off the look of the house but it is only our starter home. He says my idea just doesn’t make sense. I don’t disagree but this closet has been my dream whereas his office doesn’t fulfill anything deep like that for him. He is free to make the living room his new personal space. Is it possible that I’m in the wrong here?", "prompt_sha256": "78c5e86b654a14385974afbc462b605dad12525f568a243e88269c886a3ab795", "body_sha256": "150a89703bd601b299ff4866b56020f40b8796b81a24ffcaba46bc3e601370ae", "previous_prompt_sha256": "2bd4ee248ee0764e4417481b8f8b377b8beb2f54f6e85db3f132525b0515cb95", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P071", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (22M) have been working at a fairly new restaurant for about 6 months now.  The owners are nice and the staff get a long  well since it is a family owned business and not a part of a corporation.  I work in the kitchen along with a few other guys, let’s call the guy on fryer Evan (fake name).  Evan was this really kind guy that would go out of his way to help you, just really great guy in general.  He had a heart condition that caused him to have seizures somewhat often among other things.  Last week, Evan unfortunately passed away due to his condition and the staff/owners have been arranging things with Evans family to help him during this hard time.  \n\nEvan had passed a few days before his birthday and one of the servers and Evan had planned to do something together to celebrate it since they’d both be working on his birthday.  She had made Evan a cake prior to his death, so on his birthday all of the staff and family come to celebrate his birthday and life.  This is where ‘Fiona’ comes in (fake name).  Fiona is a server that has been working with Evan and myself for a few months now. \n\nAt the celebration, Fiona was quite upset (understandably) and was inconsolable for most of the time.  There was a few words said, mainly by the family, some staff and by the restaurant owners but also by Fiona.  Her message started off normal until it turned weird?  She began talking about how her and Evan were work husband and wife and how she will miss seeing him every time they worked together.  The issue was that Evan’s fiancée and Fiona’s boyfriend were both in attendance.  The fiancée obviously was upset from the fact she had lost Evan but now Fiona saying that she was his work wife at his celebration of life.  \n\nAll of the staff were in shock at this, Fiona was a few drinks deep and she was a bit of a messy drunk but no one had expected her to say that.  After she said this in front of everybody, another co-worker of ours managed to get the mic out of her hands and to head home.  Nobody had mentioned it for the rest of the night because of just not knowing how to process her sobbing about missing her work husband.  Today though, we had a shift together and we naturally didn’t talk that much due to working in different areas of the restaurant but she had been acting off and still very sad. I had heard from another server that she was still going on about how hard Evans death has been on here as his work wife and that she should’ve received time \n\nI’m not too sure why I took it so personally but I asked her in front of all of the staff that was working (most since it was a busier night) why she was acting like she was his actual wife.  She got upset saying I had no right to talk to her like I did, especially about Evan, and that I was a prick.  We exchanged some words then avoided each other for the rest of our shifts.  My co-workers are saying that I was unprofessional and shouldn’t have said anything to her since everybody was upset about Evan’s death and everybody mourns differently. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "b0ac080bf43238ebaa97217ca9a514f52671f0d8c04a6ecc789f75aa3dca59c1", "body_sha256": "4ac598b6e22dbcdf23bd5ab9037edc98a5f1637e576366e29fe231cfc35e6bc7", "previous_prompt_sha256": "7605202380558bb5d1b2cab30cb15721891f9c9355d7c3e6429cef069135018a", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P072", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy fiance (26F) suggested to me as a time saver for my breakfast in the morning, I should boil an egg and eat it on my way to work in the car. Now here is where I might be the AH I immediately laughed and said that's the worst idea I've ever heard and said that's fucked and laughed even harder. She immediately got upset and a big fight ensued which turned into us yelling about whether I would a boiled egg in the mornings from now on. She ended up staying at her mother's, help?", "prompt_sha256": "d2d3fb8543d02e2bb2a426e3969d36959d68c60059f8181bbbbd013717a5f18d", "body_sha256": "938ac25ba5b0c1312b83ffd4f6c2b1513986807872842d221d9070db2e9d1cce", "previous_prompt_sha256": "c64280ebf3051d97ba0869a036c1d70cc9a987eff3ff64e600d1d589363650ec", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P073", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nPeople involved:\nMe (31F)\nNieces (6F, 5F)\nHalf sister (33F) bio mum of nieces and my half sister from my dads side.\n\nMum (64F)\nStep dad (63M)\nHalf sisters (21F, 19F) \nStep brother (29M)\n\nBasic background:\nBefore my dad met my mum he had my half sister. Then he met my mum and they had me. My dad passed away when I was 7 and half sister was 9. We didn’t really see each other after this as our mums didn’t like each other.\n\nMy mum went on to meet my stepdad when I was 9, who already had my step brother. They then went onto have my half sisters. They are still together now.\n\nI call everyone mum, dad, brother, sister. I don’t differentiate by step or half.\n\nWhen I was in my early 20’s I met back up with my oldest sister. She didn’t have a good life, her mum had been on drugs while she was growing up and was a heavy drinker. She had been in and out of care all her childhood. She was struggling with her own mental health and I suspected drug abuse as well. My sister’s mum passed away before my nieces were born.\n\nI’ve been in my nieces lives since before they were born (I was birthing partner for both births), I’ve looked after them when my sister wasn’t able to, when she would sometimes disappear for days at a time and on the occasions she was in police custody/prison.\n\nThings have recently come to a low point and my sister has been arrested again and it looks like she is going to be away for a long time. We have had meetings between myself, my sister and social services. We have all agreed that it would be best for my nieces if I have special guardianship of them (it would take a court order to take my nieces away from me).\n\nThe issue:\nMy mum and that side of my family have really rallied to help me. I already had a room for the girls but they helped redecorate and they help me with child care when I’m at work and they aren’t at school.\n\nI told my nieces they can call my family whatever they feel comfortable. So either their names or anything else polite. They still call me auntie and at the moment they call my mum and stepdad, Mr and Mrs (their last name) and my brother and sisters by their first names. My family keep trying to get my nieces to call them grandma, grandad, aunts, uncle. I’ve told them to leave my nieces be. They think I’m being an asshole by not telling my nieces to call them grandma etc. If I told my nieces to do it they would.", "prompt_sha256": "41e724d912c875d0af6ebf763486b0478f0658c8009131d8289330d253100bbc", "body_sha256": "fa7e9c5e6283ecb67ced30d9639e4f48a0c772304bcfc8ee609b201185bfc684", "previous_prompt_sha256": "f330836779e9792ef98758bd1ceb08cb220e947543164572370211eb747f2f49", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P074", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nTitle basically says it all. \n\nI have a lot of trouble filtering out noise when people speak to me, so I really need people to either speak much more loudly than the noise or wait for the noise to stop before talking to me. \n\nMy partner knows this, as I've told him over and over. He continues to speak in almost a whisper or at normal volume when there are other noises and I can tell he's speaking but can't make it out. If I ask him to repeat, he repeats at the same volume and eventually gets annoyed with me and tells me to drop it if I ask him to repeat too much. \n\nWe've had so many arguments about how he needs to speak more loudly if he wants me to hear him but he never does. It also feels like he makes a point to talk to me when I'm in the shower/washing my hands/doing dishes/vacuuming, basically anytime I'm doing something that makes a sound, he'll think it's the best time to talk to me and I have to stop what I'm doing because he refuses to speak up.\n\nI'm honestly pretty tired of it and have decided that from now on if he speaks too quietly for me to hear what he's saying, I'm just going to pretend I didn't hear him at all. I'm tired of having to fight to understand him while he continues to make 0 effort. Tbh ignoring him feels really petty but I'm hoping he'll just be like \"oh she didn't hear me speak\" and either wait until I'm done with whatever I'm doing or talk louder.\n\nWIBTA?\n\n***Edit for info***\n\nI've had my hearing checked and my hearing is fine. It's processing that's the problem.\n\nMy main complaints with my partner are NOT that he speaks too quietly in general, but that he speaks too quietly when I'm either busy or in a different room AND that he gets mad if I ask him to repeat and accuses me of not listening to him if I didn't hear something.", "prompt_sha256": "831c09f84f2c3ad49388e3e2f7b0aaecdbae8031e1f308b4330e2f44e4e71868", "body_sha256": "6c801518b33695c1688906ca6ce443d431f4ebe2fd5864db67bf3091454ed291", "previous_prompt_sha256": "d39a3171de8d3730be807ec38f69f91fc3341924c2c2bc180a16dca31673f100", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P075", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis is a throwaway account for obvious reasons. It's also my first time posting on this sub so I apologize for any formatting mistakes I might make.\n\nI (27F) have a friend \"Caleb\" (25M) whom I hang out frequently. I regularly visit their house (my area lifted the covid restrictions) and therefore his family is quite accustomed to me visiting. He has a little sister (16F) I will be calling \"Melody\" and she sometimes joins us when we hang out.\n\nIt started around two weeks ago when I noticed Melody posting drawings on her Instagram. I didn't think too much of it that day, but was a little surprised since I've never seen her draw despite visiting quite often. The next time I visited, while we were talking about the small music group Caleb is a part of, I made a comment along the lines of \"Your entire family seems to be artistic, I'm quite jealous.\" and that caused a confusion, so I explained that I saw Melody's art account.\n\nMelody then proceeded to tell me how she usually reposts the art she finds on either Pinterest or Twitter as \"it is a lot better than scrolling down on the artist's profile.\"\n\nI am not an artist myself but I have been on the artist side of social media (as a mere enjoyer) enough to know that this is basically art theft, so I explained to her how this is wrong and why she should delete those reposts. I didn't think I was being harsh, but she got very upset with me and told me a bunch of stuff such as \"how can it be theft when it is right there for me to download\" and \"they keep posting other stuff on their profiles and it's annoying to scroll down\". I didn't want to ruin the conversation so I didn't push further, but admittedly, I was a little annoyed.\n\nThis is where I think I might be the asshole, I found her account and reported every repost she posted. And this resulted in a good portion of her posts being deleted and some other people commenting on posts about how she shouldn't be reposting other people's art.\n\nMelody called me yesterday while crying and told me that I ruined social media for her, the only place she made friends and had fun. I thought I was doing the right thing but after the phone call I'm questioning my decision. Am I the asshole?", "prompt_sha256": "406d5ec1466f9104a20d7fe1f1e9e603b0007a7188bb0905de9065866cb4da86", "body_sha256": "509c24002e98675b7d7d3ce7eaec69d885d14360a1f05a3d732624849fdc1b9d", "previous_prompt_sha256": "905a2f49a9eccb003c7aa1ba55a9d6d23b48be3745c7a9157864eb33edccba9c", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P076", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI F got proposed to on my birthday by my lovely fiance M.\nIt was a massive surprise and made me so happy, he proposed to me with a cute pink froggy ring which is just a temporary ring as he wanted me to be able to pick a ring myself that he knew I would love to wear which I really appreciate.\nI as anyone would told my family about it as I was ecstatic, my older sister who I have little to no relationship with decided to mock the temporary ring and whole ordeal behind my back and didn't think I would find out.\nLittle context, my older sister has caused many problems in my life with the outstandingly awful decisions she made. She has always only thought about herself and didn't care about the repercussions it would have on everyone else.\nShe  acts like she cares about me but she is a massive snake and her words are always insincere.\nI think I've just about had enough of how she has treated me that I really just do not want her at my wedding anymore, she makes me uncomfortable and I'd rather not spend my day feeling so worked up and anxious.\n\nSo would I be the a**hole?", "prompt_sha256": "d6ce8fcc1892f63f8a275a542cfed877fc9d1c058a8513ee9ba9c09d9fac7f59", "body_sha256": "90fafeb3b94f14f9fe66ff0cdd5ed5eed1b73aaa3a084d4e0134603c83781a72", "previous_prompt_sha256": "ea18890794b5040164326e79c08e0d769258cc18d6562480a2e5d9620ddda79c", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P077", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (27F) went out on a girl's dinner with my best friends (26F & 29F). For context, I'm the only one married, they are not in any committed relationships. \nYesterday we went to have dinner at a sports bar/family restaurant where, from the moment we arrived the waiter (M/early-mid twenties?) started complimenting us. He kept saying flirty/funny things. I ignored him but honestly gave me such an ick, they were giggling. After a while, as he took our order and kept refilling our drinks, he kept saying stuff like that and I did a sarcastic laugh (picture that one meme of the dude laughing and getting serious) he left the table and didn't do it again. \nMy friends later told me I was rude to him and that he was just doing his job but omg it was ruining my afternoon. But now I'm wondering if I just should've kept quiet.\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e7a8a62a9d6f7605c4d793c2e30135a67e13401d50b5493e3f8a33c86c095c42", "body_sha256": "2d613bbe84c21a87aa1a8dcb2569aef18c34d06222acb8c7cd50c595d490a48a", "previous_prompt_sha256": "bbce5ed16a56b43deffdbcc9fa607e82f899f9e0a19675f3c365bbbc5cc40680", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P078", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy wife and I both agreed that we didn’t want kids when we got married. She said that if she got pregnant she would get an abortion. \n\nWell the impossible has happened, and through 2 forms of birth control she’s pregnant. She’s saying that she can’t go through with an abortion. I said that she could go the adoption route if necessary. She said she couldn’t do that either, and that she wants to keep the kid. \n\nWhat happened to the agreement? What happened to the whole “I don’t want kids” thing?\n\nWe’ve been fighting over the past few days and she says that she’s keeping the kid. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "1a5b2929900a58dbe6980f7b4778a296726ae493d80684135db6ede1c9744e33", "body_sha256": "43b277bf90d86b36f19c00590d0c494a9a8bb27aac96cbcf2ce95667d452d9bf", "previous_prompt_sha256": "4a86f32b6dedd55b9cc2eaf096ce2c608d1ea3948bb4e30dee4fd08e47f3e255", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P079", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI, Jade (F 25) am getting married to Henry (M 25) in October, on Halloween. I am an asexual woman. Henry has of course accepted, and supported me. My family, on the other hand, has not been supportive, although they claim to be allies of the LGBT community.\n\nAfter the proposal, we began planning, the topic of bachelor/bachelorette parties was brought up. Henry and I talked, and had our party planners agree on some \"rules\" about these parties. Now I am not insecure about my relationship with Henry in any way, and have never been, and I know Henry would never ever cheat on me, and I would never ever cheat on him. As a person who had never been too fond of such parties, we decided on; 1, no strippers or anything of the sort , 2, don't drink too much (my personal choice).\n\nAs I mentioned before, my family had never been accepting of my asexuality, and liked to make fun of it, going out of their way to make me uncomfortable.\n\nSo onto today, the day of this party i've been dreading for weeks. I walk in and there are bright pink dicks everywhere; confetti, candy, the cake, and plastered all over the wall, it looked like someone grabbed any dick themed item at a Spencer's and threw it all over my living room. Barely clothed men danced around my house, so. much. alcohol. I was standing there stunned. I felt super dizzy, and the next thing I knew I was over the toilet throwing up. I just kept asking \"why\" over and over again. My cousins were laughing. I thought I had been completely clear about how uncomfortable this shit made me, and they still went and did this to me. I was pissed. When I stopped, I cleaned myself up and went into my living room to end the party. I told my cousins that I was absolutely disgusted, and felt betrayed that they went against all my boundaries, and asked that the party be ended. They laughed. So I left.\n\nIt didn't take long for them to start blowing up my phone with call and texts calling me as many curses as I had taught them in our youth, I didn't even have time to call my fiance or anything! I sat in my car, and through sobs, I called and explained to Henry everything that had happened, and he was understandably sorry and pissed at my cousins. He offered to pick me up to join his friends, but I told him that it was his day and he needed to have fun with his friends, but he insisted. When he had finished calming me down, I texted my cousin a simple \"have fun without me.\" and went to a cafe, where I'm now writing this, waiting to be swooped up and rescued by my fiance.\n\nShould I uninvite them from my wedding? Am I being too harsh? I mean, after all that, and you still couldn't get the dicks in blue? Or strippers that were my type?\n\nTLDR: My cousins went against my wishes and boundaries giving me a dick themed bachelorette party with male strippers I specifically asked for there not to be, and they got mad at me for being disgusted and leaving.", "prompt_sha256": "3a9c5f9c3efe12476e621537b5e8db2747d8d63e60512c5c98424d772220c3f7", "body_sha256": "71d323bbc857fc3565d88aa5f4274b6771b135570d36fec4290c4b22cd8189ee", "previous_prompt_sha256": "04f83a9e2455f527e890b29a0a179a66525589816fedc3e0785711d00c7d5ed9", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P080", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nOOh boy I don’t feel great about this one but this just happened yesterday. My girlfriend is pissed. Idk where to start. My gf and I both 25 have been dating for 3 years. Her best friend from high school moved to a different state after college. She got a bf about a year ago and my gf and her always talk about a double date. Her friend was in town for the weekend for the first time since before Covid. They made plans to go out to dinner and top golf and maybe a bar after scheduled for yesterday. Friend was only in town for 3 days and very busy every other day. So this was a huge deal to my gf and I do feel bad for letting her down. \n\nMy brother 27 isn’t the best dude, he’s got his vices. But he’s my brother and I love him. He’s always been there for me. He has lived with his girlfriend for the last 4 years and dated for 7. Long story short, he was cheating. He got caught by a mutual friend and was forced to come clean. I guess things got a little ugly with some shouting and the cops were called. Nothing happened with that that I was told. But ,y brother called ,e frantically and said they came to an agreement that he has 48 hours to get all his shit out of the apartment while she goes to her parents. If he doesn’t “he is fucked”. I have a pickup truck. He begged me to do it. This was on Saturday so we had to do it yesterday.  I had to tell gf I couldn’t make it. \n\nShe is very mad. I tried to compromise and ask if we could change plans to a brunch but they had plans. I also said I’d make it as soon as I was done but that wasn’t okay with her. She thinks my brother  sucks and I suck for helping. Also thinks I knew about the cheating. I didn’t have proof , but I did suspect things but didn’t really ask questions. She still saw her friend but the long awaited double date didn’t happen. AITA.", "prompt_sha256": "1a6b2e1d89a8fc7dae24ed1dfec783007ecdb3211b6430d186090357f143f17b", "body_sha256": "4ac885df9b58d0cfcd8b2d8a855fe9cbf3d74c4a806e631d4d2bb8d1a52df913", "previous_prompt_sha256": "aaeffaf84e240053f577fd220a0a467e8355bb28fdff888cfcbd0abe86423bee", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P081", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI, 19f have a sister, 15f, and 3 step siblings. 21f, 24f, and 26m. The 24 year old, who we will call Margret, has autism, but at a very low level. She cannot drive and is a little socially awkward. My blood sister, who we will call Emily, just started learning how to drive. She has her permit and Is a decently good driver for being a new driver. One night, we were all going out to dinner and Emily was driving. It was me, Emily, Margret, and me and Emily's dad in the car. Before we started driving, Emily asked everyone to be quiet so she could focus. Margret retaliated saying \"I can talk all I want\" which I replied reminding her that Emily needs to focus and that she can be quiet for a few minutes. I do admit that I said this in a slightly rude tone, but I only did so to get the point across. I was sitting in the back seat next to Margret while my dad was teaching my sister. The entire time, Margret was making rude comments about Emily's driving, acting as if she knew how to drive. Margret has driven our golf cart before and I she almost crashed id say 6 times, not exaggerating. The fact that she was trying to backseat drive when she doesn't even know how to drive was making me already want to say something. It was one comment she made about her parking when we got there that made me lash out. Emily did a very good parking job, was centered and everything, but Margret still decided to say that it was crooked and it was giving her OCD. I have actual OCD and I wasn't bothered at all. Margret has ben tested for all the things, ADHD, OCD, depression, anxiety, etc and she only ended up having anxiety. The comment wasn't even the thing that made me mad. It was the way she said it. She said it in the nastiest tone I think ive ever heard which made me scream at her and tell her to shut up because she doesn't know how to drive and will most likely never be able to drive. I do feel that I could be the asshole, seeing that she is autistic but I feel it Is nessecary to tell her what is wrong and what is okay to say. My dad, who should be communicating these things with her, didn't say anything about it which is also part of the reason I lashed out. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "5121a0711cad1398460bc2f18d1d3280b8c499c511fb20044563844ef73959a7", "body_sha256": "a4b8d9d143fb96111e3ad32e596c6b8f7907c236f1e6ebd230a4f5387d9c7b00", "previous_prompt_sha256": "ee74b1c2c65a51e06a5d6ce1a9d0d18ad333eda82aa337908e16cfbd5edce50c", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P082", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy BF and I have been together for almost 10 years. During that time I've managed to secure a very nice office job with several great benefits including a lot of vacation time that essentially accumulates indefinitely - it doesn't expire if I don't use it by a certain time. My BF on the other hand has stayed at his barely above minimum wage retail job that offers almost no paid time off and makes it very difficult for him to schedule any time away for what little he does get. As a result I've barely touched my vacation time because there's rarely any opportunity to actually go on a vacation together. \n\nMy coworkers and my boss keep commenting that I'm always working and never taking breaks so every now and then I'll take a week or maybe half a week off to just sit at home and relax, play video games, work on some hobbies. My office is super cool about this but every time I do this my BF starts acting really resentful, making snide comments about how it must be nice to just drop work whenever I want, implying that sitting at a desk all day isn't real work anyway, \"jokingly\" calling me a jerk for taking time off when he can't (\"I'm just kidding\" he says when I call him out). It makes me really reluctant to ever use that vacation time for myself because I know I'll  have to deal with guilt trips instead of being able to relax and enjoy having nothing to do.\n\nIs it really an insensitive thing to do to use my vacation perks when he can't?", "prompt_sha256": "3ae9caa2532ce523021392e0d600d7b631dc9bf9d163ca800dca73c1171af297", "body_sha256": "5d34bb5ec2f07baf37fb39837d464bb88752fc2d6f086efc923674924aa6bd5f", "previous_prompt_sha256": "29e85f5c29733fc6dab035e48703a75bb7c94204cfd7394970afbc7915a0ca5d", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P083", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo this was back on Halloween but you’ll see why I posted it now. Anyways my friend and I I(15F)were taking my three little sisters(all 8F) out trick or treating in our neighborhood. Down the street there’s a lot of ppl we don’t know cus it’s a dead end.\n\nMy little sisters are all disabled. One of them has severe heart disease which affects her pulmonary arteries and her lungs so she needs oxygen tubes. My other one has a severe lung disease and needs oxygen tubes. And my other one has osteogenesis Imperfecta and uses a walker. She’s average height and looks able bodied but her bones in her legs are so soft and have been broken so much that it’s hard for her to walk.\n\nAnyways the three of them were wearing costumes from their 100th year of school day AKA they were dressed up as old people.  They just had like cardigans on and curly grey Afro wigs. The way I did it was like I stood on the sidewalk as they walked up to all the houses. Most people knew us and the few that didn’t, didn’t say anything about the costumes or the disability aids.\n\nUntil we got to this one house. My friend and I stood by the sidewalk as the three of them walked up. When the woman answered the door I could tell she looked upset. She started lecturing them on something. I’m HOH and had left my hearing aids at home so I got closer to hear what was happening. My friend had started filming. Apparently she thought they were faking their disability and they were being disrespectful. I heard her say “I’m not giving you candy until you go back to the store and return all of this stuff for ppl who need it.” \n\nI stepped in and explained that they do need it and Mia even lifted her sleeve to show her picc line. She didn’t say sorry or anything she just gave them candy. The girls laughed ab it as we were walking away.\n\nThen yesterday i found this fb post she made on the town group that day saying that she nicely asked if they needed them and they did and then she apologized profusely. All the comments were in her support so I got the vid from my friend and posted it in the comments. Most ppl r mad at her but a few said i shouldn’t have brought it up bc it was so pong ago and I “knew how this town would react” \n\nThe post is deleted now but i still feel bad about it. AITA?\n\nEdit: they r not triplets rlly, they r artificial triplets cus they’re all adopted and born close together\n\nEdit 2: as one commenter said, I thinks he posted that bc she thought I was gonna go around telling ppl and she wanted to get her “side of the story” out first.", "prompt_sha256": "5c8221adc699640720034d4bcb63306cc657d9bc182ae4d3e18ef3f19d054d62", "body_sha256": "c825c1fce8f868c033d8c61ebeb3026561125e49a281fd306f326f0489eb0584", "previous_prompt_sha256": "0aaa9bb631f3efe280c3c6807bd38bf081d5189f4f08f635dcf15a17bff47188", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P084", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy boyfriend is currently unemployed but actively searching for a job. I try to help him by asking my friends if they can refer him somewhere or by spending my own time looking for jobs on various job sites and company career pages.\n\nI'm the kind of person who believes in \"spam applying\" when it comes to job hunting. Of course, I still check the basics like location, salary, benefits, and job description. But if I think I can handle the job, even if I don't meet the exact qualifications (like years of experience), I still apply because I believe there's nothing to lose but everything to gain. After all, you're just sending a resume or answering some assessments—aside from time, there's nothing really at stake.\n\nHowever, my boyfriend has the opposite mindset. He's in HR, so he says he understands how this works better than I do. He believes that qualifications are set for a reason, and it's fair to follow them. I get that, but I still stand by my belief that \"there's nothing to lose.\"\n\nIt's been almost two months since my boyfriend became unemployed, and responses to his applications have been slow. Sometimes, I send him job postings that require more experience than he has, but it's usually just a one-year difference. I feel like there's no harm in trying, plus I'm trying to broaden his opportunities because he has so many filters—he doesn't want to work in a BPO, and he doesn't want an onsite job.\n\nWe got into an argument about this because I was getting frustrated that he sticks to these rules so strictly, as if he's the one setting them. So I ended up telling him that he's being too close-minded. Now, he's not talking to me. I know I was harsh, and I do feel guilty because I hurt him, but I still believe he needed to hear it.\n\nSo, AITA for telling him that he's being too close-minded?", "prompt_sha256": "9ea1384f9d3aaad96e5b8500c7f42bc42b46c0277e0aa1270ccb37d564e58e7b", "body_sha256": "e0a8f5eeba632ba342b354ce86a0466ecbc3fb33de24fcd1563085688bf99c6b", "previous_prompt_sha256": "908f3fc44a404c36b46801420fb10ff03823b511f6e33d8e7f5102b85bdc567b", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P085", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy 17 year old recently got busted playing cruel pranks on one of his classmates, it involved a girl, a date, and then a series of photos of the student being stood up circulating around the school. My son fessed up to it. I gave him the choice to either write an apology letter to the classmate he 'pranked' or he could be grounded for 3 weeks. My son chose the 3 weeks, I suppose that's a pride thing. \n\nHe's spent the better part of it in his bedroom because he's been studying for assignments and exams and I was fine with that, he's always been good with his grades and he puts a lot of work into passing. About 4 days until the end of his punishment and I asked him if he'd like to watch a movie with the rest of the family, he said no, his test at school was the next day and had to study, fine by me.\n\nI'm usually at work before he wakes up (gone by 6:30) so I went into his room before bed to wish him good luck only to find his room empty!. I searched the house for him, figuring he could have gone down for snacks or to use the bathroom but he was completely gone. It was then that my husband discovered he'd cleverly removed the security screen from his bedroom window and had been sneaking out. \n\nSo, I proceeded to throw his belongings out of the window, he said he was going to be in his room and that's where he went so I figured that's where all of his stuff belonged. X Box, lamps, computer, clothes, posters, yes, even the bed was dismantled and thrown out into the backyard. \n\nWe kept all the lights on and retired to our bedroom like we always do (it was about 10pm at this point) and when I went downstairs, there was my son sitting at the table with a glass of juice, saying he came down for a study break. When he finished his juice he went back upstairs and came down a few minutes later. He didn't seem remorseful at all at being caught and merely said 'okay busted, where's my stuff' I told him it was all in his room. \n\nHe found it all outside and threw a teenage temper tantrum about how unfair it was, I told him he could either write an apology letter to us and we'd help him move his stuff in or he could move his own stuff back in provided he wanted to move back in and put it all back together himself. We got our apology letter and helped move things back in and set his room back up with everything that wasn't broken. On top of this, he had to finish off his grounding AND apologize to the classmate he 'pranked' \n\nThe grounding lifted as planned and he went to stay with my sister for the weekend in the country to clear his head. He must have told her what happened because I received a nasty phone call about how much of an AH I am and how that was way too much for such a small offense. I personally feel as though it was justified after he'd completely ignored his punishment and lied and thought he was being sly about it. \n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "d6256346b80e2f07a3e597a6614a4069e927379e1d0dfc9f281c8267aabef0cf", "body_sha256": "169232716e3feaf9c6b1887a0e034d9ae372841c9cdf39e0fedd1bb1f826273e", "previous_prompt_sha256": "a8ff3404d2dbaa1ae51b05e58ec45ff3c6c881a6688cb8c5b65dc091f456fc59", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P086", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nFor the last 3 years my husband and I have been pretty much estranged. Things were pretty hostile between us for the majority of that time. \n\nDuring that time my sister and sister-in-law (brother’s wife) were my two biggest supporters. My sister was very vocal about how she thought I was making a mistake living with him again but my sister-in-law said she would support me regardless.\n\nIt was my parent’s anniversary last Sunday and they invited everyone for a family dinner. My dad, who is very happy I’m living with my husband again, told me to bring him too. I wasn’t sure if I should since we’ve only recently started living together again and I knew my sister would be upset about it but in the end, I decided to ask him if he wanted to come.\n\nMy sister was visibly angry when she saw my husband. She kept making passive aggressive jabs at him all night and since he never took the bait, she ended up confronting him after dinner. She told my husband I was only living with him again because I was scared he would take our son away from me, which isn’t true, and that he was a bully. She kept asking him if he was happy to have a wife who didn’t love him and she told him I was too good for him.\n\nI never said anything at first because I was so shocked she was actually saying these things to his face. I feel like my husband was goading her without saying anything outright nasty himself too. My sister ended up yelling at him and my sister-in-law joined in too. My dad tried to get them to stop and so did my brother but it just made the situation worse.\n\nI ended up telling them to stop and leaving with my husband and son. The next day both my sister and sister-in-law sent me long messages about how I shouldn’t have brought him as I knew how they felt about him and that it ruined the dinner. They said just because I had stupidly forgiven him, didn’t mean they had to as well. I expected my sister to be upset around him but my sister-in-law’s reaction shocked me, I know she’s fighting with my brother now because of this too.\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e4d1fda44022c332b528846dc9ed63c35f81d73f9348e5e9ddc98164a9bbe96b", "body_sha256": "17369fecb964bd6f592782b514dab297cfc5f9f818d96ac3e919e411da56f4e8", "previous_prompt_sha256": "d3189964932fa87cdb11c879e8bf712719c696f535b570d91b5a63859339bebe", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P087", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy brother(21m) has recently moved back in with me (17m) and our single mother. He is a high-school drop out that is either extremely angry and aggressive or zen and quiet. Both my mother and brother work full time and I am a full time student. I cook and clean for the house most days, and usually take on the majority of household chores. \n\nRecently, with my school nearing an end, I have been overworked with multiple summative assignments and having to study for exams. When I have tried to ask for help in my house, the responses I get are always “I am tired” and stuff like that. It’s been bothering me as my school lasts just as long as their jobs, although when I come home I am still expected to be doing school. When they come home their day is done, yet they sit on the couch playing on their phones for hours and either refuse to help me with chores or help for 10 minutes then go back to the couch. \n\nMy frustration peaked today when I was writing a 5 page report and my mother asked me to take out the garbage. When I looked over to see her on her phone, I replied “it looks like you have time to.” When my brother heard that, he immediately blew up on me calling me rude and swearing. I called him a lazy high-school dropout but still ended up taking the garbage out. \n- I will note for extra context I have replied to her a few times like that before, although they have always just been simple “it looks like you can do it” type responses and never anything too intense \n\nAITA for talking to my mother this way when she tells me to do chores while I am doing homework or studying?\n\nEDIT: I’ve seen a lot of comments about my mother paying for my life. I’m not sure if this matters in context but the majority of my mothers income is paid from my father for me, she does not pay out of pocket for me to live here. As well, the house we live in was purchased by my fathers family so he knew he children would have a house to live in.\n\nUPDATE: I tried to talk to my mom about at the very least asking my brother to do chores sometimes. Or perhaps organizing a chore chart. She started crying and yelling at me that I have ruined the atmosphere of the house. I know now I WAS THE ASSHOLE for being rude. Although I don’t think I am wrong to want more help around the house", "prompt_sha256": "6ded0aeecfb5a308052035796618f69ed07ceade7ad919e05729ae68e0d45916", "body_sha256": "67e1b2a02637a7b7590a0b36aab6462234d542e3528360426be0d60bcac296d7", "previous_prompt_sha256": "2fafc1fe75adbe263a37570c89ab129678c88320cf8e3f87fb572553aaaccc2a", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P088", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (28f) have to have a scheduled c se ction to deliver bub #2. \n\nMy 3 year old has horrible separation anxiety if she's not with dad (34m) or myself. \n\nI really do not want to go through this c s ection by myself , I want my husband there with me at the hospital I dont want to do this alone. \n\nSo we've arranged for DD to stay with her grandparents while we are in the hospital \n\nMy parents are willing to watch DD but say because she's not used to being away from us that I'm being selfish and should have DH stay home with her and one of them will be in delivery with me, but DH should not miss the b irth of his own child. \n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "698488012d8243cc5822d0c72d83813cac35dba2ac785d109efabc21696c935c", "body_sha256": "3aeb4bc8f66aa3f126284595a3d8a3cdf2872b1af52e28e1b277156085c8eaac", "previous_prompt_sha256": "87608f12dd2a0d0d979974384674851fce318ac8775acd7daf2e079c435e1a1d", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P089", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo my roommate told me a few days ago that she planned on moving out. I asked if this was her 30 day notice? And she said no, she doesn’t have a definite date just around March or April, maybe. Then asked if I wanted my gf to move in. I said probably but I’m going to have to talk to her about it and make sure everything is going to work out with her being able to afford to move in with me.\n\nSo my roommate jumped the gun and told our property manager that she’s leaving and that my gf is going to be added to the lease. Annoying because I never gave her the ok to do that. She gave me two options. Pay her out her half of the deposit or pay her half of the rent. I told her I’m not doing either since she hasn’t given a exact move out date. Ever since then things have been pretty awkward with her. She’s been making it obvious that she is pissed off. \n\nSo It’s the first and I asked did you put in your 30 days? Or are you waiting till April. She said in a very annoyed tone that no she didn’t put in her 30 days cuz she hasn’t figured out a date yet and to have my gf sign that lease ASAP. I told her to not worry about my gf cuz we got offered a really good deal on a place somewhere else and won’t be staying. As a courtesy to her we will wait till she puts in her 30 days. That way we both will have the same exact time to move out and won’t have to worry about one or the other staying behind to deal with the full rent or paying the other person out.\n\nShe flipped out. Walked away and we didnt even finish the conversation. I’m thinking she’s upset that I’m not going to be giving her the deposit right away or paying the rent fully like she planned. And now she feels pressured to get a definite move out date. She’s been walking around slamming downs, cupboards and giving me the cold shoulder. \n\nI don’t see why she would be so upset about this. But she’s definitely making me feel like I’m the asshole for not staying \n\nAita?\n\nEDIT: I appreciate everyone’s thoughts and input. After talking to my gf and a my close friends who know my roommate and know the kind of person she is...we came to the conclusion that she wants my gf on the lease right away so that she could take her name off it and not have to worry about a time frame to move out since she wouldn’t be on a lease anymore. And she wants us to give her her half of the deposit because she can’t afford to move out before getting it back. I asked roommate if she even has a place in mind to move to and she hasn’t even started looking so it confirmed that she was just trying to get out of a lease and pay as little as possible.\n\nEDIT EDIT: I called and put in my 30 day notice. A bit of backstory to show y’all the type of person I’m dealing with. We met each other through a mutual friend and we only moved in together because we both had a timeframe to find a place and couldn’t cover moving cost by ourselves. Everything was good the first month until I noticed she wasn’t replacing communal items like, toilet paper,trash bags, paper towels, or even food that wasn’t purchased by her but she ate. She wasn’t even cleaning up after herself. Dishes were piling up, moldy food on the stove, she would even leave bloody pads stuck to the bathroom floor. I called her out on it and things went down hill from there. She then moved in her barely 18 yr old gf (roommate is mid 30s). When I asked about splitting the bills since there were now 3 of us. She refused to have her gf pay anything cuz technically gf wasn’t on the lease. She told our mutual friend that she’s planning on moving cuz she can’t afford to take care of the gf and pay her half of the bills. So she’s moving out with the gf so that the gf will have to contribute. Ever since the first incident where I asked her to clean up after herself, I started to compile a list with pictures of everything she damaged beyond repair. I’m asking for a detailed bill in regards to the deposit and I’m subtracting everything she has broken from it.", "prompt_sha256": "509de8430a3b73c785f3c9ee3745c284316f7ee9af3a6d440c52f7b49d1e0242", "body_sha256": "4fd7026c7d47640ce721ba87757fdf381416c19eb38cb545699401384f501640", "previous_prompt_sha256": "5f5d129495fc23a7f3b7e67dd6914777db9c0534e2fcce605e13c5921f9acec7", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P090", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (25m) live with my girlfriend Kelly (22f). She's very sweet, resourceful, and hard-working. She had a full-time job and let me move into her apartment. I quit my job a few years back and I've been struggling to find another one. I've applied almost everywhere but everything is taken. Kelly was honestly a blessing because of how much she helped me during my own financial situation. \n\nKelly, however, has been recently diagnosed with depression and anorexia nervosa. She had to go inpatient once due to her mental health issues. During her stay there, I took care of basically everything in the house, including our two cats. Once she got home, she told me she had wanted to get a part-time job as she goes through recovery, and she requested me to get a part-time job as well to help around the place. I agreed to do this, but I was still struggling. \n\nMonths later, we are almost overdue on rent because of Kelly's reduced income. I kept trying to find a job, but there were none I liked nor did they take me in. Kelly hasn't pushed the idea, but she has recently brought up that I should get a job to help around the place. I kept telling her that I'm trying, but finding one isn't easy. \n\nDays later, Kelly started having a bad day. I tried hugging, kissing her but she wasn't having it. She was really annoyed with me too and told me straight up to get off my ass and get a job like I promised. I found this uncalled for and very random. I told her I'm trying but she said I'm not and have been slacking for months. I replied that it me getting a job is not even getting us rent then she should listen to her own advice and get a full-time job. \n\nShe said I'm a lazy joke and locked herself in our room. Was I the asshole here? I'm trying.", "prompt_sha256": "667c8fedd812a7d264e168006882b543873ad8ebd72d7a21fef6b7df1ac1dd4a", "body_sha256": "672c96cb5ecc9278b1c3e010dd497ef905fcd62c662b43970ace8561631b7289", "previous_prompt_sha256": "0b98177ef62ed211eeba71cd8ac7e8ddbce52637a16599be1be60db7c6bd3428", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P091", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy bf quit smoking cigarettes before we started dating because it was a deal breaker for me. Almost 2 years later, everything is at a high in our relationship, I caught him with a juul in his pocket. He was doing so well off nicotine I didn’t want him to get addicted again. I asked him to stop and give me the juul. He gave it to me and I ended up putting it in one of my bags. A month later, I find that he went behind my back and went through my bags to find his juul, and has been smoking behind my back whenever I’m not around, and lying to me about it. I caught him once after I noticed it was gone, and I was upset, I reminded him that he promised me he would stop. As soon as I mentioned this and he got caught he just says “omg here we go again”. And he shuts down and leaves. Refuses to have a conversation about it. Every time I try to address it he shuts me out and is very sarcastic. So now I’m just not talking to him until he owns up to his lying and has that conversation with me. We haven’t spoken in days. We live together.", "prompt_sha256": "baedc283286cef81328165f9c658ac7cc248cc74c810b9a7231252fe99eab7a8", "body_sha256": "8529340d92fc2f25a7e6313eb9c4454a44de4bfabbbc3cd7097a9b8bf97755d0", "previous_prompt_sha256": "de0a6a1b04bb2240a41c9c630dd093d01c0893cdfa1523bf52046ed9cc0a3fd7", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P092", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis is such a petty argument but im catching it from all sides so I need to know if I was really the asshole in this situation as my mom, sister, and nephew all think that I am.\n\nRelevant information: My mom and I share custody of my niece whose 7. She is special needs and attends a private school on a scholarship because of it. At this school breakfast, snack time, and lunch all have to be provided by the parents. \n\nOnto the issue. My mom and I buy my niece snacks for school in bulk to last the month with foodstamps. My nephew is significantly more well-off than we are and is EXTREMELY frugal.\n\nBecause of my  moms open door policy regarding family members and food he will come to our house MULTIPLE times a day for food and drinks. He'll invite himself over for meals and eat more than his share as well as take home plates for leftovers leaving us with no leftovers ourselves.\n\nBut I draw the line at my neices snacks because they serve a purpose and we need them to last. But every. damn. DAY. He is over  taking her snacks, so much so that sometimes he'll even eat all of a particular snack before she's even had a chance to have any.\n\nWe've asked him multiple times to stop, she herself has even asked him to stop and in response, he'll call her greedy and spoiled. That she's not eating them so why can he have some. Like duh she's not eating them right now they're for school!\n\nEverything finally boiled over for me a few weeks ago when I learned that he literally took food off of her plate and called her greedy and said she needed to share because she asked for a donut that happened to be the last donut in a box and \"she knew he wanted it thats why she asked for it\"\n\nSo today he took the last of her Halloween brownies my mom bought as a special treat for her and that caused her to cry. Mom didnt say anything about it so she came to me and I called him out for taking the last brownie. \n\nHe got pissed and said she's spoiled, greedy, not the only grandkid, and he can eat here if he wants to. Then threw the brownie in the trash and stormed off. \n\nSo was I the asshole?  \n\nThere is alot more to the situation but due to the character limit I can go into more detail about everything that happened before this.\n\nEDIT: my nephew sent me this text a minute ago: \n\"I just got y'all snacks a few days ago. It's not like I'm coming over every day and eating all of y'all's food. You need to teach Jenna to share with people instead of being that fucking stingy about some snacks. \n\nIts terrible behavior for Jenna to act like that and do that fake cry about a snack she wasn't even eating. If your that tight on money that you want to come screaming at me over a 50¢ snack cake then y'all need to really get your finances in order.  \n\nThere's plenty of food in there so y'all can't be starving that bad.  It was WRONG what you and Jenna did to me. I already know you won't care but I won't offer y'all snacks anymore and I won't eat y'all's food. It was honestly ridiculous you even did that to me over a snack cake. \n\nY'all get food stamps and shit I don't. It's also wrong that you encourage her with that type of behavior too. \"", "prompt_sha256": "18245b34baae580eb01869ab4b831766a5394a5730b955a7d25e73f16b086da4", "body_sha256": "3b672892c9154917e1d32d501096f70d5c7f99f57c470b0256269e5f1d5c4e90", "previous_prompt_sha256": "7bd6993e5b02290529c3619507d35fda3eb29d4d59067b6728302a4725e9471e", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P093", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis is my throwaway account. And English isn't my first language, so excuse my mistakes.\n\n\nFew days ago, I got a call from unknown number and it turned out to be my dad's friend who isn't VERY close to my dad. He talks with my brother (I guess) and got to know that I'm planning to study abroad after finishing College in my country( I did call my brother after that and gave him an earful). It seems like he wants his daughter to study abroad (Just for name sake) and wanted me to decide on where I'm going and what I'm going to study  so that he can send his daughter with me to study together. He also mentioned her daughter doesn't mind whatever course I pick because she isn't into studying that much and just wants to have some fun.\n\nFyi, I still have one year left till I complete my college and I haven't thought of next step even though it's time for me to start preparing something like GMAT,IELTS/TOEFL.\n\nHe offered to send me videos and info about different courses which I didn't want to initially but since he compelled me, I thought he was just trying to help and it wouldn't hurt to learn more about programs which might suit me. \n\nThen, He started to call me everyday (2-3 times per day, I ignore sometimes)and asked if I made my decision. Again, I guess I have enough time so I didn't want to finalize yet.  He also started to convince me into Counseling services and much more stuffs which I wasn't interested in. I politely told him that I'm already consulting someone else and I'm not interested in what he is sending me. Soon, I felt like he was pressuring me and not helping actually. So I decided not to take his calls and respond to any of his texts. \n\nInstead, he called and told my dad about everything and asked him to make me make decisions soon. My parents aren't pressuring me (which is a good thing, since I get anxious very easily and he's making me very anxious, which Is another reason why I'm avoiding his calls) but my dad is wanting me to talk to him again just to escape his calls. If I don't pick up his calls, he instantly calls my dad and talk for a long time(which annoys my dad too but doesn't wanna say). \n\nMy dad wants me to deal with him myself. Mind you, I haven't even talked with him before even though he claims that he came to my home one time( maybe I forgot) but, still it doesn't give him rights to talk/ pressure  me like this.", "prompt_sha256": "ccd8a1adb62dfd37f817a1d4a58e56c48a7855c657cc6d7d1760023a2b5ccb0a", "body_sha256": "6d71394b0796f973d27cd3e1f1aa5cf6a8f4e3419da60108542eac9943c52849", "previous_prompt_sha256": "469ed84964f2f7e415563052335c4e6327ec978d999ce75957e0869c9fc997d0", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P094", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (42f) daughter (15f), while extremely intelligent, has severe ADHD (inattentive-type) and as a result can be very forgetful sometimes. For example, she loses a lot of things and will forget to take care of certain basic needs unless we remind her (think drinking water or using the bathroom). It can get frustrating since aside from that and some other learning differences she's a pretty smart, normal kid, but her father (47m, ex-husband) and I trust that she's working on it and usually help out when we need to.\n\nYesterday she and I went on a day trip to the beach. It was pretty overcast for most of the day, so I didn't remind my daughter to put any sunscreen on when we got there (thinking that it wasn't a huge deal anyway and if she wanted to wear some she'd remember herself). She only remembered about the sunscreen as we were leaving. By the time we got to her father's house, her skin was bright red.\n\nHer father called me this morning to tell me that she has sun poisoning. While I'm very sorry that this happened (I would NEVER want my daughter to get burnt so badly), he's accusing me of neglect, saying I should have reminded her because I \"know how she is\". I understand that she has ADHD, but she's not developmentally disabled. She needs to learn how to look after her own needs, and I don't think not coddling her over every thing she does makes me a neglectful parent (especially when I took her to the beach for a whole day). However, she's in a lot of pain, and I feel like I could have done more. AITA?\n\nEdit: I just want to say that this was a genuine accident. It'd be so so so cruel for me to purposefully not tell her to put on sunscreen to \"teach her a lesson\"; I would never knowingly put my daughter in danger like that. I just expected her to remember on her own (I could see how that was a mistake now).\n\nI did put on sunscreen before we left, but only a tiny bit, and I didn't reapply at all during the day because I thought it wasn't a big deal due to the weather (another reason why I didn't push her with the sunscreen). ", "prompt_sha256": "00716d20151ba2caadfeaa7126c5358cbab66760e1457a51f84c5a9f9f8d8104", "body_sha256": "60d3feb0b2ea588bb70c508917a318a0c13576d2abc11a00e22366ba4f8e29b4", "previous_prompt_sha256": "8862a3db2d1597725576baec9e227d6cd5abe831694f6308eb0a6c9619053b2e", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P095", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (30f) sister in law (25f, brothers wife) always takes the biggest bowl when she comes over for dinner. I'll frequently host 4-8 people and make dinner. When dinner is ready I'll set it out for my guests to grab their own food along with any dishes and cutlery they'll need. I only have a couple giant bowls and the rest are standard size.\n\nEvery time, my sil will disregard the bowls I've set out and will grab the biggest bowl in my cupboard and fill it. She'll always get the biggest helping out of the entire group but won't always finish her helping. So now I'm stressed that not everyone will get a sufficient amount of food.\n\nI do have a tendency to be a bit fussy and kind of controlling which I've been working on. So I'm trying to see if it's that or if she's genuinely overstepping.\n\nUpdate: thank you all for your responses! I'm gonna take the overwhelming advice and just hide the big bowls the next time she comes over.", "prompt_sha256": "bf808fb4669f8b047cf829a4eda711068c3dbd9db8921a30b0a55d2991539f2a", "body_sha256": "f1345d649d79e2cbb5c1a7a29d498fa194441c02df4278053dcc24ddfafa0143", "previous_prompt_sha256": "718613f2bb5ef483d43086d2eb555f246d6dc3776b3429798859081bad48f292", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P096", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis is my catch all anon AITA account.\n\nI (23F) am 100% AH for ruining a friend's jacket. I didn't know who it belonged to, but I used it without asking, and there were stains left on it. I don't recall there being stains on it, but after I told my friend I used it she called me to say I left stains. I genuinely get that i should have asked first. I also know I should have taken more care, and although I stand by the fact I left it in the condition I found it, I know my friend isn't lying.\n\nBut that's not why I'm here.\n\nThe stains haven't come out and the jacket cannot be dry cleaned. The company no longer stocks the jacket, so we went looking online for similar items. The original jacket was about $80. I sent her similar items, and offered to pay $100 regardless if the item was cheaper than that.\n\nI didn't hear back from her for about a week, and today she sent me a link to a jacket for ~$240. It's very similar to the other options. I said it wasn't reasonable to ask me to pay that considering the original cost $80, and I had offered to pay $100.\n\nShe said I owed it to her because it would be payment for the lost time without the jacket. I just said I'd be happy to pay up to $120, but I wouldn't pay 3x the original cost especially because other, cheaper options were just as similar. In fact, I would argue this option is the least similar to the original.\nShe said I was cheap, a thief, and I did this to sabotage her.\n\n\nI know I'm going to get a lot of comments saying I shouldn't have used something that I didn't have permission for, and I fully acknowledge that. However, I need to know whether it's reasonable she's asking for 3x the cost, especially when there are cheaper options that are just as similar in style and material.\n\nAITA for standing firm on my $100 (now $120) offer?\n\nEdit: a few people assumed I just chose cheaper alternates, but let me clear things up. It wasn't on purpose the options were cheaper. I didn't specifically look for cheaper options. Objectively the jacket she has chosen is the furthest from the original. The options I found were on Amazon because they were the only ones that I found, whereas she found a high street option. Her original jacket came from a local store, but it was definitely very cheap. One of the options I found on Amazon shared an image with the one on the original site (only one, the rest were different).", "prompt_sha256": "e1fa90373c69e13b77c09dcbcecd4e401460b513dc7f7c829f2906e3ec774285", "body_sha256": "901f7a0e6e2d8077d609e7b4b16adeb1a74069e51d60b6a0308a066bef692bc6", "previous_prompt_sha256": "f6de9a0c1621c04defba6b2ac3b532b1a1e1cdce82d3cc0426f837a63f558b7a", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P097", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nFor the last six months my brother (21m) would have a whole bottle of vodka every night after work. I (18f) told him he must stop or i will tell our mother. Every night for the last six months he has repeatedly said “tonight is my last night”. \n\nA couple of days ago, I told my mother, she was completely upset because she is devout and threatened him with being kicked out. \n\nHe has been upset with me and is still doing it every night, blaming me for him carrying on. \n\n\nAITA for telling my mother?", "prompt_sha256": "9a21c9ed58426f0ae5a9a4ccc5271ccd429e48fc74628c29f50eda89e12454c6", "body_sha256": "91fccad88be7a6c66c63387486194fcf0b5d10e5173f8261551720dbcc1d9f99", "previous_prompt_sha256": "d522c8d95322da4877b48ae584519fab199194b0c488ba3e2bbdff90ebf47495", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P098", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI'm Irish. A decade ago I met Ex. 2 years in I got pregnant. We married, and when our daughter was born he let me pick her name, so I gave her a very Irish name. Fake name I'm using is Saoirse, and the real name is different but similarly Irish and hard to say unless you've heard it already.\n\nEx's mother (MIL) would ring once a week and come to Ireland a few times a year. I always ended up cooking/cleaning for her (she'd stay with us), and when she was on the phone Ex would say \"do you want to speak to OP?\" and I'd have to talk to her. I didn't like this because she hated me, as she was very anti-Irish, and anti-me by extension.\n\nEventually I told Ex that I was done with MIL. He and Saoirse can keep talking to her, but if she calls then don't put me on, and if she comes to visit she can get a hotel and they can go meet her.\n\nA few years ago Ex and I began to have problems. Eventually he asked me for a divorce. The custody agreement we ended up with gave me majority custody, but he gets summer holidays and every other Christmas. He was moving back to England and asked if he could still have contact with Saoirse, so we worked out a schedule for him video calling once a week for 30 mins. He's remarried, his wife is pregnant, and the number of calls from him has been going down, which doesn't surprise me as it's a tricky pregnancy.\n\nAs he's been calling less MIL has been using his skype account to call us in the time slots he isn't using. Because it's a video call on my laptop I can hear everything, including MIL calling Saoirse by the name \"Sue\". I didn't say anything on the call but after I asked Saoirse if that was the first time MIL did that and Saoirse said that MIL gave her an \"English name\" but she didn't like it. I asked some follow ups and found out MIL also corrects her speech when she uses Irish dialect and asks her to tone down her accent.\n\nI was fuming but didn't do anything until the next video chat where I heard MIL call her Sue, and then I asked Saoirse to go wash up, took her seat, and said \"you know her name is Saoirse, right?\" MIL says it's hard to pronounce. I say it's not and break it down to sounds (Sur-sha) for MIL. MIL says the English name is easier, and I say that's no use if it's wrong and told MIL that if I heard MIL call her \"Sue\" or correct her speech again then I'd reconsider this setup.\n\nNext video call was last night, MIL immediately greets her as \"Sue\" I then pop my head in again and say \"I warned you\" before hanging up and blocking Ex's skype account.\n\nI ignored the incoming video calls (she used her skype and her and Ex's facebooks) for the rest of the night. Today I woke up to several messages from Ex saying I shouldn't have hung up on MIL like that and I need to unblock the account, then call MIL and apologise. I had a bit of a moan to my cousin who was on my side until I told her I hung up on MIL and says I should apologise for that only.\n\nAITA?\n\nInfo: MIL has 2 other children in her life, unsure of her relationship to them, but their names are Iona and Lachlan, both of which she pronounces fine, so this really isn't a case of my daughter's name being \"too hard\".\n\nEdit: fuck it. Her name is Roisin (pronounced Row-sheen). She also goes by Rosie. MIL is insisting on calling her Ruby because when my daughter pronounces \"Ruby\" her accent goes funny and sounds more English.", "prompt_sha256": "fdb0f69a58f2e69ba36bfd2fb6a7bc873ff8acaf100124da1362cf39d75c0b76", "body_sha256": "695dff2861c6a743754b426ecd4a7a6d47efdb98633d0173521ea6faaabd2eb9", "previous_prompt_sha256": "960787041e20d9121481bd3b6ad40bbd235849f62b096df39a6493ceaa6b1a5e", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P099", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy fiance just had birthday and my mom asked if she should bake him a  cake. I told her that it is not a good idea because he is extremly picky eater. She insisted on baking it. I gave her a specific instruction to make sure it would be something he would actually eat. I told her to make a lemon flavoured cake with no butter cream because he hates butter with passion and not to make it overly sweet. And i specifically said no fondant, because it is just overly sweet and disgusting. We also found a refrence picture.\n \nFew weeks went by and it was time of the birthday party. My mom proudly gave him the cake and i was horrified when i saw it. It looked nothing like it should have. It was also coverd in fondant and had a thick layer of butter cream. My moms explenation was that she had to use butter cream because the other cream was melting the fondant she wanted to put on top. Also the cake was plain and not lemon flavoured, but the cream had a coffee flavour. Excellent choise for someone who hates coffee. When my fiance asked what it is made of she lied about the butter cream and told us to remove the fondant if we do not like it. We told her she should keep the cake and eat it since she did not listen to the given instructions and we would most likely not eat it. She insisted we take the cake. So we did. We tries the cake and neither of us did like it, so we ended up throwing it away. \n\nNow my whole family says I am an A-hole for ordering a cake and not wanting it anymore. The say we are ungrateful because my mom spent lot of time and effort making it and we did not apriciate it. So am i/are we the A-holes?\n\nEDIT: He has gallbleder removed and has to follow a specific diet.", "prompt_sha256": "87bb8828aed33c97a6207f7a97c8df7e05e9fb5671911f23b46b17ede57b103b", "body_sha256": "4b27a6035ea0343503e17aa206e935dc965e90ac903b1f210ee10162fc3e6af8", "previous_prompt_sha256": "81e0439f3106b107c8d89ebc87089e3b9b4c338cc3e66a1c6bbf3ada3eeef82f", "word_limit": 61}, {"stimulus_id": "P100", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite no more than 61 words in total, including the judgment label. You do not need to use the full word allowance.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (17m) am disabled. I have a condition called Ehlers-Danlos syndrome which, in short, weakens my connective tissues and causes severe chronic pain and hypermobility among a myriad of other symptoms. I see a number of specialists for this condition, one of which briefly prescribed me mild muscle relaxers (tizanidine) to see if they would help at all. They didn't, so I stopped taking them, but I'm only able to see that doctor about once every two months, so I kept getting refill bottles that I wasn't taking. My mom, who has a history with drugs and other substances, started taking them since I wasn't- it didn't really sit right with me but I figured no harm no foul since I didn't need them and would've just thrown them away. \n\nA little while ago, I saw that doctor again. I mentioned to him that the tizanidine wasn't doing anything for me- important information I felt like my doctor should know about my chronic illness. So he took me off of the medicine. My mom *freaked out* about this- she immediately started going off about how I'm incredibly selfish for \"cutting her off\", how I'm just an awful child because I won't ever do anything for her or to help her out, how I obviously don't care about her well being because she \"needs them\", how it's not fair and I need to tell him I want to go back on that medication again, etc etc etc. She keeps bringing this back up and telling me she's really upset with me and going on about how I \"never do anything for her\" and \"god forbid you just do one nice thing for your mom\" and everything in that vein. I feel really guilty but I don't want to lie to my doctor and do something that's technically illegal just so she can take some muscle relaxers. \n\nI feel like I'm going fucking insane. I shouldn't have to LIE to my doctor to get her drugs.. right? Am I an awful son for not being willing to do that? I guess technically it wouldn't really hurt me to lie about it but i want it marked correctly in my chart that muscle relaxers don't help me because my condition is kind of serious... I don't know. I just want a second opinion, I genuinely feel like I'm going crazy here. Thank you for any and all input.", "prompt_sha256": "e617bd89d8c2585b4eb9995b9c1f6f83721a730794069d3ff94f219b89b424e4", "body_sha256": "6257ae2ab1c81ef642e8b843eb26a9cef0a8057281de40c54bad646677609fac", "previous_prompt_sha256": "f932baa13c7dda59e886e8af5dac048b253d67a0a029a197027d6e96fdb50b15", "word_limit": 61}]$materials$::jsonb)
 as x(stimulus_id text,prompt_text text,prompt_sha256 text,body_sha256 text,previous_prompt_sha256 text,word_limit integer);
